{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e","id":415418,"title":"Exigents are my biggest concern for 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-22T11:15:42-08:00","id":415418,"title":"Exigents are my biggest concern for 3e","content":"Now alot of people love the idea of exigents, and to me thats the reason I am worried. It reminds me alot of devil-tigers which overwhelmed infernals to the point the original concept was essentially ignored. Please indulge me as I get out my more bias baseless concerns before I express my narrative and conceptual issues of it.<br /> <br /> I can already see the concept drastically overwhelming the player base with ideas. Everyone is so obsessed with their special snowflake exalted that the actual splats might as well not exist. Calling back to devil-tigers, when they were introduced pretty much everyone wanted to play one to the point non-devil-tiger infernals essentially didn't exist. In fact infernals didn't exist they were just a needed speed bump into becoming a primordial. I imagine the same thing happening. No one will be playing solars or lunars because why do that when they can be the one of a kind chosen of whoever that has the exact themes I want for a character.<br /> <br /> That brings me to my more legit issue. Limitation breeds creativity. This is the point of table top RPGs. You are given a system and you must work within the system to get what you want forcing you to look into alternative methods. Exalted did a great job of giving you limited tools but ones versatile enough that as long as you don't mind some compromise you can still do alot of stuff. A solar cant just sprout wings like a lunar, but he could craft an artifact to give himself wings of essence, or use his charms to just levitate, or wyld-shape permanent ones. Not exactly what you wanted but mixed things up. Its good to have a sense of, you need to work with what you've got. Solars cant shape-shift, lunars cant alter fate, etc. Thus you need to get creative.<br /> <br /> Exigents defeat this. Why think up clever work arounds when I can just have him be a chosen of a god who embodies exactly what I want. No god like that, fine I homebrew one that is and it completely works within the setting. At that point you might as well be playing a free form RP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:43:06-08:00","id":415476,"title":"","content":"Devil-Tigers were very much designed as a patch to cover up the fundamental design problems of Infernals. Their resemblance to Exigents is quite superficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:46:50-08:00","id":415482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now alot of people love the idea of exigents, and to me thats the reason I am worried. It reminds me alot of devil-tigers which overwhelmed infernals to the point the original concept was essentially ignored. Please indulge me as I get out my more bias baseless concerns before I express my narrative and conceptual issues of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there are similarities between Devil-Tigers and Exigents. I think something that will help is that the insane high-Essence stuff of Devil-Tigers is not going to be a baseline concern for Exigents. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can already see the concept drastically overwhelming the player base with ideas. Everyone is so obsessed with their special snowflake exalted that the actual splats might as well not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how this matters - this is a table-level thing, not something that will affect what books are put out. An ST is entirely within their rights to say &quot;Solar only&quot; or &quot;only 1 person can play an Exigent&quot; or whatever. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling back to devil-tigers, when they were introduced pretty much everyone wanted to play one to the point non-devil-tiger infernals essentially didn't exist. In fact infernals didn't exist they were just a needed speed bump into becoming a primordial. I imagine the same thing happening. <br /> <br /> No one will be playing solars or lunars because why do that when they can be the one of a kind chosen of whoever that has the exact themes I want for a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a table-level concern as well. Ban Exigents at your table if you don't want to muck with them. That is completely fair. Ban Devil-Tigers if you don't want the huge headaches that exist from having to gen up an elder Essence Charmset from scratch. That doesn't mean they're a canon-level mistake (well, Devil-Tigers were only in that if anything in late-2e was still trying to hew to the Bronze Age aesthetic, Devil-Tigers basically showed that that was not important to the line at all anymore).<br /> <br /> And I disagree with your premise that nobody is going to play anything else. I think Exigents are cool but I know there are going to be a LOT of times where I won't want all the work of creating a Charmset and want to play something fully-printed, <i>or I just plain want to play a Solar or Lunar</i>. I have a friend who is completely uninterested in anything but Sids and Infernals. Etc. <br /> <br /> I am looking forward to Exigents first and foremost as NPCs, especially because constantly fighting DBs as your Exalted opponents can get tedious. Exigents add a ton more capability and unpredictability for STs to use as antagonists, both in combat and socially. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents defeat this. Why think up clever work arounds when I can just have him be a chosen of a god who embodies exactly what I want. No god like that, fine I homebrew one that is and it completely works within the setting. At that point you might as well be playing a free form RP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguments from incredulity are a logical fallacy. And that's not how freeform RP works either - that kind of thing generally has no or few actual mechanical rules, and Exigents are going to be as mechanically heavy as all the other splats. So....no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:16:23-08:00","id":415526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please indulge me as I get out my more bias baseless concerns</div> </div> </div> </div>Please indulge me as I quibble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one will be playing solars or lunars because why do that when they can be the one of a kind chosen of whoever that has the exact themes I want for a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this happens, then the problem is &quot;why do Solars and Lunars&quot; suck so much, no one wants to play them?<br /> <br /> The &quot;I want you all to enjoy my brand of beer, so I forbid you from bringing your own&quot; tactic is a shit one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limitation breeds creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a weird statement, since you then admit that a Solar - lacking wings - can just forge an artifact to fly. This isn't creativity. And in truth, the core splats (especially Solars) often have charms to bulldoze themselves through any problem.<br /> <br /> Most creative White Wolf game I recall.... was Vampire the Masquerade. :P Disciplines were linear charm-trees that only went 5 deep (you'd need Essence 6+ to approach the clouds from levels 6-10). Each clan only had 3 innate Disciplines (the rest you'd have to learn, <i><b>if ever,</b> </i>from rival clans somehow). In Exalted terms, a Solar-Nosferatu would have a single Athletics excellency; 5 lowbie Stealth charms; and some weird Survival charms <i>and that's it; </i>a Toreador has 5 Presence charms, 5 Auspex (a weird Investigation / Occult hybrid) and 1 Dexterity charm (for multiple actions). Your charm kits were <b>much more limited</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>There</b> you had to be creative. I remember a lowbie who wanted to kill a bunch of Vampires at Elysium (a sort of gathering). His <b>only</b> power was lvl 1 Obtenebration (create and manipulate shadows). They all out-powered him <i>drastically</i>. This was a PVP friendly game that was starting to drag because a small number of players had really powerful elders and none of them wanted to retire.<br /> <b>Sooooo</b>...... this guy's phone keeps going off, when others are talking, until the Assamite uses Quietus on him (with a charm to create silence). Next thing you know, someone's head gets blown off. The splattered blood makes the Brujah (a short-tempered Vampire type) frenzy on the Ventrue (the leader, sustaining order); the Nosferatu then begins exchanging blows with the Brujah; a fire breaks out, throwing the sane into Rotshreck; the Toreador is stunned in silence at an <i>orchestra of slaughter</i>.<br /> <br /> How'd you bring a gun in here? Brought it in pieces.<br /> Well.... we would have heard you put it together! Nope. Other guy used Quietus on me.<br /> Well.... we would have seen it! Nope. Obtenebration. My only power. You can't see what I'm doing in my coat.<br /> Well.... why'd you do it, it makes no sense! Nope. I deliberately shot the Assamite so the splatter makes the Brujah frenzy. <br /> Well.... there's a fire, you should be freaking out! Nope. I'm just a ghoul. Mortals don't panic at fire. <br /> <br /> A ghoul (think of a ghost-blood or Abyssal Half-Caste or even Heroic Mortal) with <b>one</b> power killed a half dozen elder Vampires (think of full Abyssal Exalts) by putting together a ripple-effect of <i>other people's powers and weaknesses</i> (all PCs) so that they ended up killing each other (or crippling each other enough for him to finish them off afterward).<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: And this &quot;reset&quot; was a welcome one, afterward, since all the players expressed relief --- the &quot;Elders&quot; all wanted to play new characters, but were afraid of giving up their old toons and being left behind by the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents defeat this. Why think up clever work arounds when I can just have him be a chosen of a god who embodies exactly what I want. No god like that, fine I homebrew one that is and it completely works within the setting. At that point you might as well be playing a free form RP.</div> </div> </div> </div>As above..... <i><b>Exalted </b></i>defeats this, because they have charms for every kit.<br /> <br /> Exigents - depending on power-level - might actually offer more of a challenge.<br /> <br /> Some &quot;small River god&quot; needs a hero and chooses me. But it needs a hero because a shadowland is spreading and Abyssals roam the land. How the fuck do my water powers help me against the dead? They don't. <br /> <br /> A &quot;God of the Hunt&quot; needs a hero and chooses you. But the god doesn't need a hunter - it needs a scholar and diplomat who can visit the local city, find out why they're switching to farming, see who is causing this change and how can he restore his worship? How do <b>you</b> solve a scholastic or diplomatic situation with arrows?<br /> <br /> Exigents aren't Devil-Tigers. We don't get to pick our entire suite, unless you're metagaming like hell/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:16:28-08:00","id":415527,"title":"","content":"My biggest concern is that I'm going to run into some player who won't be interested in any of the default splats and isn't mechanically savvy enough to build their own exigent, thereby forcing me to do all the work of character creation beyond the concept phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:20:30-08:00","id":415531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415527#post415527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is that I'm going to run into some player who won't be interested in any of the default splats and isn't mechanically savvy enough to build their own exigent, thereby forcing me to do all the work of character creation beyond the concept phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>An easy solution - steal charms from other splats.<br /> <br /> I built my first Martial Art by mixing-and-matching canon charms from existing styles, making them into something <i>new and unique</i>. It made it easier for the ST to approve (because they were powers we had access to anyways, in the books) and any future errata could be applied to the charms, if necessary.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't treat Exigents as something for <b>the players</b>.<br /> <br /> I'd consider Exigents as something for <b>the storyteller</b>.<br /> <br /> You want to tell a certain kind of story. Create a certain kind of Exigent. <br /> Mere mortals aren't so lucky to choose which god chooses them.<br /> Use these new powers and kits to ensure no one punches your plot to pieces with a single Solar charm.<br /> <br /> Or as I said above:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some &quot;small River god&quot; needs a hero and chooses me. But it needs a hero because a shadowland is spreading and Abyssals roam the land. How the fuck do my water powers help me against the dead? They don't. <br /> <br /> A &quot;God of the Hunt&quot; needs a hero and chooses you. But the god doesn't need a hunter - it needs a scholar and diplomat who can visit the local city, find out why they're switching to farming, see who is causing this change and how can he restore his worship? How do <b>you</b> solve a scholastic or diplomatic situation with arrows? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:25:41-08:00","id":415535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415527#post415527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is that I'm going to run into some player who won't be interested in any of the default splats and isn't mechanically savvy enough to build their own exigent, thereby forcing me to do all the work of character creation beyond the concept phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>In such a case I think it might be better to either say &quot;I am not willing to do this much heavy mechanics lifting in building your character, so I'd rather you not play an Exigent and stick to a splat with more published mechanical support&quot; or just not invite that person to play.<br /> <br /> Kinda sucks, but as an ST if you feel forced into this position it's likely the game is going to have OOC problems before it even starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:26:18-08:00","id":415536,"title":"","content":"Well, most of the time (on the rare, <b>rare </b>opportunities I get to play instead of ST) &quot;the exact themes I want for a character&quot; means &quot;a Solar&quot;. Likewise, I won't bother creating, say, any kind of &quot;Sidereal plus&quot; when I want the play experience of being a Sidereal. any &quot;plus&quot; to that experience is not really a bonus at all, since it instead pushes away that experience.<br /> <br /> Besides, Exigents are cool and all, but, at least as far as my table seems to be concerned, &quot;I want a unique snowflake&quot; syndrome is nowhere near as prevalent as you seem to think. Of course, your own experiences may differ and, if it is a problem, just forbid Exigents. Or, if the players are at least OK at homebrew and won't make you do all the work, let them have their damn Exigents. As long as the specific Chosen they want to create works with the themes and &quot;power level&quot; of the game the group is running, there is really no reason why you couldn't have a Circle of Exigents. It is no more strange than the multitude of mixed-splat games people have run at their tables.<br /> <br /> As for limitations and creativity, I don't see the big deal. For one, it requires creativity to come up with an exigent in the first place. One likely must have the creativity to invent an interesting god, then the creativity to extrapolate how that god's powers, themes and personality stretch into a full Exalted Charmset. Second, limitations will still exist. No ST worth their salt is gonna allow the Exigent of &quot;the god of whatever I want to do now&quot;. Just because the player invented a god, doesn't mean that god has no thematic constraints. So, the player gets the theme they truly want, but have to work within the constraints of that theme, just like everybody else who really wants to play any other exalt type. Just don't let the Chosen of the God of snakes grow wings and shoot fire from their eyes and you should be fine XD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:29:28-08:00","id":415538,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as an ST, wrestling with 5 players who all want their own homebrew charmsets, and in fact even as a player who's making his own homebrew charmset from scratch, it's hard and often tedious. It can be fun once or twice, sure, but it can take weeks to write up something that everyone can agree on.<br /> <br /> Also exigents HAVE to have a theme. You can't just say &quot;I'm the exigent of the got of shapeshifting and fate and the five elements and also he's Solar in power and can wield the power of the Wyld too because he's Wyld tainted.&quot; If you want to be a wind exalt with solar level power you can do that, but you can't just split into whatever else you want.<br /> <br /> I've also been told that exigents &quot;just don't work like that.&quot;. Which is also what I've been told when I brought up how evocations let a Solar bedecked in starmetal weave fate like a spider, or packing some serious white jade to do all the cool things that normally an earth aspect could do. We'll have to wait for the book to actually see though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:34:58-08:00","id":415548,"title":"","content":"I like Exigents, they're an awesome idea.<br /> <br /> I'm still gonna be playing primarily Lunars, Solars and Alchemicals, because Exigents don't come with the things I want to play with - A loose association of rebels against the realm, the returning god-kings that symbolize the hope of Creation, or dependence on Communism and infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:37:12-08:00","id":415549,"title":"","content":"Exigents are, presumably, not all that numerous. Throughout most of Creation's history it was easier to either ask the Solar deliberative for help, ask local DBs for help, barter with the Sidereals for aid, or find elementals, create god-blooded, or persuade mortals to help you. Exigents are a desperate measure utilized by gods in dire straits who either manage to get the Unconquered Sun's approval or who recklessly go behind his back. This is not exactly common.<br /> <br /> There are maybe a few hundred Exigents in Creation at any one time, probably less (my personal choice is ~200, which is less than there are Lunars), of wildly varying power levels. Insofar as they represent a potential problem, it is a manageable one.<br /> <br /> There are potential pitfalls with Exigents, yes, in that they allow a min-max focused player what is essentially a pre-optimized maximization pathway. However, to date Exalted has always been exceedingly vulnerable to 'optimization' approaches destroying the setting and while the 3e devs are doing their best to build safeguards from what has been released so far, will probably continue to be so, just not quite so egregiously. The storyteller system has always required STs willing to say 'no you can't do that' especially at chargen.<br /> <br /> With exigents it probably makes sense as a rule of thumb to outright ban any empowered by war gods or other directly martial deities and to simply state that Creation's top 100 gods already have enough exalted muscle at their command (through Sidereals and DBs) that they simply do not need exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:47:11-08:00","id":415560,"title":"","content":"Yeah, limitation does breed creativity. Of a sort.<br /> <br /> You probably will see fewer people playing a Solar or Lunar and trying to work them around to a style that isn't that catered for by the splat.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's necessarily bad, or less fun.<br /> <br /> There's still a lot of ways to indulge creative problem solving in a game without the constraint of trying (for some reason) to make the character do things which another splat is able to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T12:59:23-08:00","id":415575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415549#post415549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are maybe a few hundred Exigents in Creation at any one time, probably less</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, I don't think this is true. I think authors have said there will be thousands - though probably not as many as there are DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:02:32-08:00","id":415580,"title":"","content":"I hope that they are as axillary to the game as was promised. I don't want to play a game with them. That's not the type of exalted I go in for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:10:49-08:00","id":415584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415580#post415580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that they are as axillary to the game as was promised. I don't want to play a game with them. That's not the type of exalted I go in for.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that Liminals and Exigents are somewhat optional like Alchemicals - you're not going to have to retcon a ton of setting history if you choose not to include them in your games in the same way that you might if Solars never existed. <br /> <br /> And that Getimians are really only important to the 3e story of Sids, but easy enough to ignore their existence too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:34:32-08:00","id":415604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415549#post415549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With exigents it probably makes sense as a rule of thumb to outright ban any empowered by war gods or other directly martial deities and to simply state that Creation's top 100 gods already have enough exalted muscle at their command (through Sidereals and DBs) that they simply do not need exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Why? No, seriously, why? The Charmset is being brewed up from scratch regardless and the ST categorically has final say. If someone hands in Charms for a war god's* Exigent that look exactly like a Dawn's but better, and the ST isn't cool with that, that's got a date with the veto pen.<br /> <br /> * With a reminder that &quot;war/martial deity&quot; is way less useful than the particular war/martial deity in question. Ahlat is very different from Siakal and their respective hypothetical Chosen would reflect those differences, even if there's <i>some</i> overlap. Likewise, even if those particular Exigents were &quot;Solar level,&quot; I'd expect both to look and feel quite different from a Solar Dawn Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:40:00-08:00","id":415606,"title":"","content":"My impression was that there were only about 100-200 exigencies and not all are in an Exalt at any one time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415527#post415527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is that I'm going to run into some player who won't be interested in any of the default splats and isn't mechanically savvy enough to build their own exigent, thereby forcing me to do all the work of character creation beyond the concept phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's too early to be sure Exigent charms will be so diffiult to make. One of their primary uses is to be NPCs. So their &quot;charm creation matrix&quot; will probably be designed to let STs create charm-trees as easily as possible. Me, I'm hoping it also can be used for good guidelines for making balanced Devil-Tigers as well.<br /> <br /> Devil-Tigers are pretty different from Exigents, though. They were so popular partly because the Infernals were given a crummy deal as a splat with the stuff about Yozis being able to spy on them and inflict Torment on a whim all the way from Hell. As long as the Celestial and Terrestrial Exalted in 3E aren't mechanically hamstrung, I don't predict <i>every</i>body ditching them for Exigents. I'd be more concerned about everyone ditching Abyssals for Liminals, unless Resonance is successfully fixed to be less unfun.<br /> <br /> I also think that a good ST will require any Exigent (or Devil-Tiger) to have a theme and limits. The Exalted with the broadest breadth of what they can do are the Solars, whose theme includes &quot;excellence at using Abilities and Sorcery.&quot; Nearly anyone else is likely to be more restricted. Remember that although Exigents as a whole can be nearly whatever, any one particular Exigent will be limited to the theme of their god, who won't be an Incarna with a huge purview like Sol Invictus has. I also think Mechalich has a good point about what kind of god would make an Exigent in the first place: the wider their purview, and the greater their power, the less likely they are to be existentially threatened enough to need an Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-22-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:47:11-08:00","id":415608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415549#post415549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With exigents it probably makes sense as a rule of thumb to outright ban any empowered by war gods or other directly martial deities and to simply state that Creation's top 100 gods already have enough exalted muscle at their command (through Sidereals and DBs) that they simply do not need exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, do what you want at your table, I sincerely doubt this will be canon and also hope it will not be.<br /> <br /> Empowering an Exigent can diminish or even destroy the god granting the blessing. There is not a real worry about that power being spammed or used casually. <br /> <br /> And, lol, &quot;need.&quot; When has not needing something but wanting it ever been enough to deter someone from a goal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415606#post415606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression was that there were only about 100-200 exigencies and not all are in an Exalt at any one time.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not a hard cap on Exigents. There is a process by which a god can request the flame of the Exigence and this is by no means a sure thing, but AFAIK there is no statement akin to the &quot;there are 100 Sidereals&quot; rule for Exigents.<br /> <br /> Also I feel like 100-200 is way too small. I'm betting on several hundred at least. There's a reason the Realm and Sids have an interest in Exigents and are relatively unaware or apathetic about Liminals by comparison: part of that is Hundred Gods Heresy related and part is likely to be volume and interference caused.<br /> <br /> I think it's too early to be sure Exigent charms will be so diffiult to make. One of their primary uses is to be NPCs. So their &quot;charm creation matrix&quot; will probably be designed to let STs create charm-trees as easily as possible. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415606#post415606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me, I'm hoping it also can be used for good guidelines for making balanced Devil-Tigers as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Devil-Tigers are even remotely a concern for 3e right now. And I hope they never are - along with ubiquitous magitech and the constant power creep with new supplements, DTs were a nail in the coffin of Exalted's baseline sword &amp; sandals themed play. I don't think the devs want to see that happen again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415606#post415606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the less likely they are to be existentially threatened enough to need an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope to see some gods who want it, and don't super-duper need it but see the Exigent as insurance against a rainy day. Sure, they'll be diminished, but they'll also have an Exalted champion. That can pay off in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:49:20-08:00","id":415609,"title":"","content":"Generally, I have faith in the basic human instinct of laziness for this to not be a problem. Most people really can't be arsed to write a complete charmset from scratch - getting people to write three paragraphs of backstory is already problem enough as is! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:33:54-08:00","id":415722,"title":"","content":"I don't know how much work it would have to be.<br /> <br /> Sure Exigents *can* be really different to classics, there's not really a rule they must be (?).<br /> <br /> A lot of the existing sets could be fairly easily reskinnable for an Exigent to get started with, and then make it the rest up as you go along, create a new Charm a week, you're sorted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:47:05-08:00","id":415730,"title":"","content":"Like, to go on with this, if you're making a Janest type Exigent of the Field God, then I assume you, if you want, roll up a bunch of generically Exaltedly skill boosting Charms, stuff that you just need to be reasonably &quot;viable&quot;, so long as it doesn't actually jar with the harvest, and throw in a few very evocatively harvest oriented signature Charms you've thought of that make your character feel legitimately *of* the harvest, and then take it from there.<br /> <br /> Not every part of the Charmset needs to be ultra mechanically unique? So long as you're having fun then great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:46:34-08:00","id":415796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I feel like 100-200 is way too small. I'm betting on several hundred at least. There's a reason the Realm and Sids have an interest in Exigents and are relatively unaware or apathetic about Liminals by comparison: part of that is Hundred Gods Heresy related and part is likely to be volume and interference caused.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that Liminals and Exigents are somewhat optional like Alchemicals - you're not going to have to retcon a ton of setting history if you choose not to include them in your games in the same way that you might if Solars never existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>These two statements are not compatible. Either Exigents are few in number and a modest addition to the setting, or they are numerous and drastically alter the power dynamics from the Shogunate to the present. These are exalts that are more powerful and (mostly) longer-lived than DBs, much like celestial exalts, every exigent matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:56:43-08:00","id":415802,"title":"","content":"I personally think Exigents will be a great addition to the game-line. However, I will almost always (when I'm not the ST) play a Solar or Abyssal because I enjoy their themes and focuses. There are a lot of people like me who may experiment with Exigents, but who's hearts will always be with a core splat. There is also a lot of things Exigents just can't do. Exigents will never have the organization or bond with Fate that the Sidereals do. While it is possible for an Exigent to be somewhat diverse, nothing in Exalted has the Lunars level of diversity. No Exigent will be able to match a Solar in that Solar's chosen area of expertise (see below).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415526#post415526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some &quot;small River god&quot; needs a hero and chooses me. But it needs a hero because a shadowland is spreading and Abyssals roam the land. How the fuck do my water powers help me against the dead? They don't.<br /> <br /> A &quot;God of the Hunt&quot; needs a hero and chooses you. But the god doesn't need a hunter - it needs a scholar and diplomat who can visit the local city, find out why they're switching to farming, see who is causing this change and how can he restore his worship? How do <b>you</b> solve a scholastic or diplomatic situation with arrows?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely true. The example we were given shows that Exigents are more diverse then we think. John and/or Holden posted an example of an Exigent of a God of Healing. This Exigent was said to be a good doctor, but not as good as a Solar who focused on being the best doctor in Creation. However, the Exigent would also be able to &quot;heal&quot; bonds of trust and loyalty between people. To &quot;heal&quot; relationships damage by politics, and perhaps &quot;heal&quot; the land where some jerk dumped the equivalent of toxic waste. So Exigents will have a pretty diverse charm set. I mean, look at Janest. A God of a Wheat Field transformed her into an Exalt capable of &quot;reaping&quot; far more then grain from a field. She wiped out a small army of fey single-handedly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:58:16-08:00","id":415804,"title":"","content":"If a player wants to run an exigent in my game they'll need to justify it with me. I understood my players being interested in Devil Tiger. Those characters ,and their players, were power hungry little psychos and the options to become what amounts to a god on steroids appealed to them. That it was a part of the infernals just meant it was an option for them to pursue, so if I was letting them play an infernal and they got that far they could go for it. <br /> <br /> Exigents are, as has been pointed out, theme bound and created for a specific purpose. So I mean an exigents powers will be based off the god who made it and the exigent itself is going to have a job straight out the bat because they were literally made for it. Even then there's differences in how an exigent will perform based on creating god. Like a volcano god in one culture might be this kind of life thing, because volcanic soil is more fertile and the eruption/lava flow clear away things to make room for new things. So an exigent for that god would have powers in line with the idea of destruction being a necessary part of creation. As opposed to a volcano god who operates on the level of &quot;eruption means F you and die!&quot; That exigent is probably going to be more destruction oriented. Even then you need to justify why would this exigent be involved with the rest of the players? I mean I don't think exigents are getting made for nebulous threats like the Deathlords, so what is the cause your character was empowered for that this being believed in strongly enough to potentially kill it if not rip off one of its limbs? Plus I would also rule that while I'm willing to help with designing the abilities on an exigent someone wants to play if they aren't putting in the work on it then its not happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:11:31-08:00","id":415811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415804#post415804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understood my players being interested in Devil Tiger. Those characters ,and their players, were power hungry little psychos and the options to become what amounts to a god on steroids appealed to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A correctly designed Devil-Tiger is no more powerful than a Solar, notwithstanding all the hyperbole about &quot;becoming a Primordial.&quot; All the fears I can remember reading about Devil-Tigers (especially the Path of a Thousand Whispers) being &quot;overpowered&quot; spring from forgetting that they're still &quot;solaroid&quot; and meant to be limited to that power level. That unfortunate charm called Yozi Cosmic Principle contributed to the confusion, too.<br /> <br /> An Exigent shouldn't be more powerful than a Celestial Exalt, either. Power-hungry gamers may be attracted to the idea of building their own charmset, thinking they can overload it, but if they aren't willing or able to make it balanced and the ST doesn't have the time to balance it for them or the patience make them balance it, then the ST is justified in making them play another splat.<br /> <br /> Same thing with making an Exigent that doesn't work well with the rest of the group. Since Exigents are one-person &quot;splats&quot; they don't run in circles of their own kind. That means that it will require additional care to design one that fits into a circle of whatevers and can work with them and the stories they want to tell, without clashing, being useless, hogging the spotlight, or trying to drag the game in a direction different from what everyone else wanted to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-22-2015, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:32:28-08:00","id":415823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415811#post415811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A correctly designed Devil-Tiger is no more powerful than a Solar, notwithstanding all the hyperbole about &quot;becoming a Primordial.&quot; All the fears I can remember reading about Devil-Tigers (especially the Path of a Thousand Whispers) being &quot;overpowered&quot; spring from forgetting that they're still &quot;solaroid&quot; and meant to be limited to that power level. That unfortunate charm called Yozi Cosmic Principle contributed to the confusion, too.<br /> <br /> An Exigent shouldn't be more powerful than a Celestial Exalt, either. Power-hungry gamers may be attracted to the idea of building their own charmset, thinking they can overload it, but if they aren't willing or able to make it balanced and the ST doesn't have the time to balance it for them or the patience make them balance it, then the ST is justified in making them play another splat.<br /> <br /> Same thing with making an Exigent that doesn't work well with the rest of the group. Since Exigents are one-person &quot;splats&quot; they don't run in circles of their own kind. That means that it will require additional care to design one that fits into a circle of whatevers and can work with them and the stories they want to tell, without clashing, being useless, hogging the spotlight, or trying to drag the game in a direction different from what everyone else wanted to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was speaking from a narrative standpoint. As in &quot;So how did your last campaign end?&quot; &quot;MY character became a reality unto himself and accomplished his dream of kicking a third circle demon in the nuts before leaving for the Wyld.&quot; Not actually having the power of a Primordial at their disposal. We play Nobilis when we want to play with the full Primordial power level thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:40:52-08:00","id":415827,"title":"","content":"Ah, you mean, making other characters and Creation/the setting irrelevant? Being in-drawn to the point of being non-interactive? I don't see that as specifically a power-gamer thing but yeah, it is a valid problem for how some people might want to play Devil-Tigers. It isn't how I would play one, though.<br /> <br /> And probably impossible for Exigents, even the ones that do have an apotheosis coming, since they're empowered by gods instead of Primordials. Creation could become irrelevant to them but only as a result of moving the game to Yu-Shan or something.<br /> <br /> As for punching a Third Circle in the nuts, well Solars and probably Lunars and Sidereals did that too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:27:06-08:00","id":415903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415796#post415796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These two statements are not compatible. Either Exigents are few in number and a modest addition to the setting, or they are numerous and drastically alter the power dynamics from the Shogunate to the present. These are exalts that are more powerful and (mostly) longer-lived than DBs, much like celestial exalts, every exigent matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really.<br /> <br /> That's one of the great things about the game re-structuring for power curves that make regional goals challenging and easy to make the entire focus for games, as opposed to the old default being you start out working on a regional goal and graduate to something global.<br /> <br /> For Exigents, I think that more is better to a degree. There are thousands upon thousand upon thousands of god in Yu-Shan, let alone in Creation. Only a couple hundred of them having Exigents would be a little screwy.<br /> <br /> Also maximum lifespan is truly unimportant given how 99.9% of Exalts don't die of old age. And the power levels of Exigents vary wildly. So...your assertions are alternatively not correct or not relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-22-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:09:26-08:00","id":415944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415827#post415827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, you mean, making other characters and Creation/the setting irrelevant? Being in-drawn to the point of being non-interactive? I don't see that as specifically a power-gamer thing but yeah, it is a valid problem for how some people might want to play Devil-Tigers. It isn't how I would play one, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't view it as a power game thing. The character just wanted power and well there was what he saw as the pinnacle right there.Kind of like how in some Dnd games you'll have characters where the end result was that the character becomes a god. For Infernals that was an option through Devil Tiger. I know Exalted isn't Dnd I'm just saying sometimes that's how a character goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415827#post415827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And probably impossible for Exigents, even the ones that do have an apotheosis coming, since they're empowered by gods instead of Primordials. Creation could become irrelevant to them but only as a result of moving the game to Yu-Shan or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> More than likely. I do hope you didn't think that was something I was saying I viewed as an exigent thing. I was saying I viewed it as a thing the Infernals did because they thought the idea was interesting. As far as exigents go I was saying I don't think the appeal is great power it just the ability to be something different maybe a different narrative type than the other exalt types.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415827#post415827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for punching a Third Circle in the nuts, well Solars and probably Lunars and Sidereals did that too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No that was just something the character wanted to do because he could really hold a grudge and didn't take people acting like they were better than him well. This probably should have been expected since one character viewed using the bathroom as a sign of weakness that needed to be expunged from the world.<br /> <br /> As for the other things being discussed I imagine number varies depending on the situation of the world. I mean like I could see a number like 1 or 2 hundred exigents being a possibility in say a hypothetical version of the 1st age that was near paradise. Because in that case you'd be dealing with exigence that just didn't go away or die (your reincarnators, your excaliburs, your bloodlines, those things) and exigents created to sure up emergencies where someone was needed right now and the response time from any of the other forces was too long. In a situation like the middle of the portion of the Great Contagion where the Balorian Crusade was happening I wouldn't be surprised if you could count the number of exigents in the world by how many legions you could make out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:21:18-08:00","id":415952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415804#post415804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents are, as has been pointed out, theme bound and created for a specific purpose. So I mean an exigents powers will be based off the god who made it and the exigent itself is going to have a job straight out the bat because they were literally made for it.<br /> ...<br /> Even then you need to justify why would this exigent be involved with the rest of the players? I mean I don't think exigents are getting made for nebulous threats like the Deathlords, so what is the cause your character was empowered for that this being believed in strongly enough to potentially kill it if not rip off one of its limbs?</div> </div> </div> </div>This may sometimes present an obstacle, but perhaps not as large a one as that makes it sound. They're still Exalted: one of the principles of that is the power they've been given can't be taken back. If an Exigent isn't interested in fulfilling the reason for being Chosen, or even just wants to do something else for a while, there's only so much the god can do about it -- particularly if that god already gave its life. While this does mean that most gods are going to select their Exalt very, very carefully, there are still going to be some in desperate straits who did the best they could at the time. Never mind the plentiful stories where a powerful entity makes a very careless or foolish choice in empowering someone and proceeds to pay for that in spades.<br /> <br /> Even then, there's the nature of the purpose: some are more transient than others. Look at Janest and Ten Sheaves. He Chose her because of an imminent Fair Folk attack. Should she rout them all, the story of what she does next -- and of what response the other disparate forces of the world have to this new Exalt -- becomes pretty wide-open. It's been mentioned that Sidereals in the Bureau of Destiny have working with Exigence- and Exigent-related matters under their portfolio in the new edition. That'd be straightforward enough of an 'in' by itself.<br /> <br /> I just don't think getting an Exigent to join up with a group of other Exalts is all that hard. I mean, to put it in perspective, remember that the &quot;assumed default&quot; group is a perfect Solar Circle. That assumes 5 out of ~150 reborn Solars all happened to encounter one another and decide to work closely together. Given that as the baseline difficulty, incorporating an Exigent into a group doesn't feel like much of a challenge to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweaking wording a smidge. 02-23-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:23:55-08:00","id":415986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415609#post415609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, I have faith in the basic human instinct of laziness for this to not be a problem. Most people really can't be arsed to write a complete charmset from scratch - getting people to write three paragraphs of backstory is already problem enough as is! :P</div> </div> </div> </div>EX: Me, I am never going to sit down and make an entire charm set from scratch. I like what the Exigents are and what they add to the game but they aren't something I personally want to try and play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:59:23-08:00","id":416104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can already see the concept drastically overwhelming the player base with ideas. Everyone is so obsessed with their special snowflake Exalted that the actual splats might as well not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;This idea is too cool for those dumb assholes who play the game, because they'll just fuck it up&quot; is one an RPG designer must never entertain. They have to credit the people who buy their product with being both willing and able to play the game. If you don't trust people that much, then it sounds like a problem specific to (though not necessarily <i>exclusive</i> to) your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:33:29-08:00","id":416170,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I feel about Exigents. On the one hand, I really like the idea of champions of gods and spirits being a diverse and varied bunch, and of heroes who aren't perhaps as earth-shattering as the Celestial Exalted running around getting into trouble.<br /> <br /> ...on the other hand, that's sort of the role that the Godblooded and the Demonblooded and the Ghostblooded and the Feyblooded have always filled in my stories. With spirits and mortals getting hot and heavy all over Creation, I'm not sure that I really need to add &quot;the Fire of the Exigence, stolen or given freely by the Unconquered Sun&quot; to the setting to justify these characters. I'm not sure it really adds that much in terms of themes or feel that wasn't already covered by a supernatural heritage, especially given that a spirit can (as of 2E anyway) grant somebody Godblooded status through certain blessing-charms. Champion of a Forbidden god or Chosen Defender of the Harvest or Sweet Volcano Dude are already things that fit under the &quot;supernatural parentage or blessing&quot; purview pretty well.<br /> <br /> I expect I may just use the Exigent-creation rules to create unique and interesting godblooded PCs and NPCs. Which I'm fine with!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 02-23-2015, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:42:40-08:00","id":416223,"title":"","content":"I admit, after Exigents I likely won't be playing any other Exalted. Maybe I'll give Liminals a spin...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:52:57-08:00","id":416230,"title":"","content":"I fear that their existence will further dilute an increasingly crowded space of Exalted. There are already hundreds of solars, lunars and abyssals. A hundred sidereals and half a hundred infernals. Then there are thousands of terrestrials. <br /> <br /> Then there are thousands of god bloods and likely a few hundred awakened mortals (though probably no longer a thing in 3rd). The field of supernatural mortals is getting crowded Already without the addition of yet more Exalted types added to the mix.<br /> <br /> What i will likely do with the Exigent book is use it to create customized Godbloods.. I havenalways wanted more detail on godbloods and awkened mortals in general, so that is probably what i will do with that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:07:46-08:00","id":416240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416170#post416170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how I feel about Exigents. On the one hand, I really like the idea of champions of gods and spirits being a diverse and varied bunch, and of heroes who aren't perhaps as earth-shattering as the Celestial Exalted running around getting into trouble.<br /> <br /> ...on the other hand, that's sort of the role that the Godblooded and the Demonblooded and the Ghostblooded and the Feyblooded have always filled in my stories. With spirits and mortals getting hot and heavy all over Creation, I'm not sure that I really need to add &amp;quot;the Fire of the Exigence, stolen or given freely by the Unconquered Sun&amp;quot; to the setting to justify these characters. I'm not sure it really adds that much in terms of themes or feel that wasn't already covered by a supernatural heritage, especially given that a spirit can (as of 2E anyway) grant somebody Godblooded status through certain blessing-charms. Champion of a Forbidden god or Chosen Defender of the Harvest or Sweet Volcano Dude are already things that fit under the &amp;quot;supernatural parentage or blessing&amp;quot; purview pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. This is how i have always seen godbloods in the game. Any god that feels he or she needs a representative in the mortal world can simply procreate with a mortal, then when their progeny is ready, appear to then and give them their mission. They run the risk of free will getting in the way, but that is a problem even with exaltation, so there is no additional risk here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I expect I may just use the Exigent-creation rules to create unique and interesting godblooded PCs and NPCs. Which I'm fine with! </div> </div> </div>You and me bother brotha. You and me both...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:31:00-08:00","id":416253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of the great things about the game re-structuring for power curves that make regional goals challenging and easy to make the entire focus for games, as opposed to the old default being you start out working on a regional goal and graduate to something global.<br /> <br /> For Exigents, I think that more is better to a degree. There are thousands upon thousand upon thousands of god in Yu-Shan, let alone in Creation. Only a couple hundred of them having Exigents would be a little screwy.<br /> <br /> Also maximum lifespan is truly unimportant given how 99.9% of Exalts don't die of old age. And the power levels of Exigents vary wildly. So...your assertions are alternatively not correct or not relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's hundreds of exigents, or worse a few thousand of them, then they are <i>everywhere</i>. Creation is big but not limitless. A properly designed region in 3e considers the influence of the following exalt types (in order of ubiquitousness): 1. dragon-blooded 2. Lunars 3. Sidereals. 4. Solars 5. Fair Folk 6. All others (with likely only one other splat occupying a given space at a significant influence level).<br /> <br /> If there are 100-200 or so Exigents they fall into the all others group and STs can safely ignore them if they wish to. If there are 500+ Exigents then they leapfrog not only Solars but also Sidereals in terms of design space importance. At that point (and geometrically more so if there are thousands) every region has to be designed with the long-term influence of powerful <i>and unique </i>exalted in mind, which becomes very challenging because the capabilities of exigents are so varied. What the average DB, Lunar, or Sidereal represents can be modeled fairly effectively and there are numerous long-running examples. Each exigent, by contrast is adding a wild card to your setup.<br /> <br /> And maximum lifespan is not irrelevant, because even if most exalts don't die of old age (though your percentage is way off, as dragon-blooded account for over 90% of all Exalted and roughly 1/3 die of old age, so a good ~30% of exalted do die of old age) lifespan of the 1% who do become powerful elders who drive setting design space matters. Dragon-blooded only live a few hundred years (exceptions exist) and therefore the deeds of say, any given Shogunate-era dragon blood or early Second Age dragon-blood who didn't leave lineage are erased by time. By contrast almost every single elder Lunar and Sidereal has a personal influence on the setting. Exigents will inevitably add another layer onto that, but if there are hundreds of them, it quickly becomes an overpowering layer - especially in the second age when their relative power is much greater.<br /> <br /> Everything the Devs have presented has suggested a greater role for both the Realm and the Lunars. There have been no suggestions of Exigents as playing a massive collective role in Creation's history. The best way to reconcile this with their capabilities and with any sort of continuity with earlier editions of exalted is to have small numbers of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:04:25-08:00","id":416273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416230#post416230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear that their existence will further dilute an increasingly crowded space of Exalted. There are already hundreds of solars, lunars and abyssals. A hundred sidereals and half a hundred infernals. Then there are thousands of terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're forgetting Liminal Exalted, Getimian Exalted, and Holden and Morke have said that there are going to be other Exalted out there as well. We know there is some sort of anti-Lunar Exalted (similar to how the Getimian's are anti-Sidereal). Plus I believe the Niobaran League had its own Exalted, though those are (presumably) extinct. And there are probably more types of Exalted on top of that.<br /> <br /> All things considered, if you don't like more Exalted in your setting, the Exigents are just one grain of sand, and probably the smaller issue. Since each Exigent is a unique being, with their own personal, individual agenda, I think they put less pressure on the setting than new Exalted groups (like Gitimians) who presumably have some sort of goal that they work towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:08:19-08:00","id":416275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416253#post416253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything the Devs have presented has suggested a greater role for both the Realm and the Lunars. There have been no suggestions of Exigents as playing a massive collective role in Creation's history. The best way to reconcile this with their capabilities and with any sort of continuity with earlier editions of exalted is to have small numbers of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents aren't really a collective splat though. Individual Exigents have probably had an impact on parts of the setting. But each one is a solitary hero.* It's not like Exigents will necessarily be working together in any sort of collective like the Silver Pact or the Realm or the Sidereal Exalted. So it's only natural that they would have had less impact on the setting, as they're not working in concert the way that other Exalted do.<br /> <br /> *Edit<br /> <br /> So okay, that's not entirely true. You can have Exigent bloodlines who pass Exaltation down to their children. But those bloodlines would never get too large or expansive. The Dragon Blooded have held the reigns of Creation since the Usurpation, and they aren't likely to brook any rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-23-2015, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:23:57-08:00","id":416285,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I don't like the idea of Exigents, or indeed of any new Exalted types. Partly because that it breakes the rule of five (Yes, I know, so do Infernals and Alchemicals, and I don't let them in games I run either) and partly because I think it runs the risk of over populating the setting with Exalted the way that the World of Darkness games are overpopulated with supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:28:47-08:00","id":416288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416253#post416253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything the Devs have presented has suggested a greater role for both the Realm and the Lunars. There have been no suggestions of Exigents as playing a massive collective role in Creation's history. The best way to reconcile this with their capabilities and with any sort of continuity with earlier editions of exalted is to have small numbers of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Exigents have even fewer reasons for group cohesion than most exalts. I mean hell its been a point mentioned several times Exigent exalt is just the category of exalt its the same as Terrestrial, Celestial, or Primordial. But an Exigent class exalt will have different powers depending on who empowered it which will also differentiate it from even other gods of a type (Ahlat and Saikal being different types of war god for example.)So the powers will be different and from there what kind of person they exalt will differ. Its unlikely that a Solar will be exalted from someone with no ambition beyond working his fields. A harvest god might exalt someone with no ambition beyond working those fields because they feel the person will be good to handle the problem without the risk of drawing more ire after the problem is solved.<br /> <br /> Plus I wouldn't be suprised if a decent percentage of exigents are listed in the books as &quot;slain anathema heretic.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T03:13:40-08:00","id":416326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416273#post416273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're forgetting Liminal Exalted, Getimian Exalted, and Holden and Morke have said that there are going to be other Exalted out there as well. We know there is some sort of anti-Lunar Exalted (similar to how the Getimian's are anti-Sidereal). Plus I believe the Niobaran League had its own Exalted, though those are (presumably) extinct. And there are probably more types of Exalted on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I havent forgotten about Getimians or Liminals. I include them in the category unecessary filler. I'm not 100% decided if i dont want to use them, and that will greatly depend on their role in the setting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All things considered, if you don't like more Exalted in your setting, the Exigents are just one grain of sand, and probably the smaller issue. Since each Exigent is a unique being, with their own personal, individual agenda, I think they put less pressure on the setting than new Exalted groups (like Gitimians) who presumably have some sort of goal that they work towards. </div> </div> </div>As mentioned earlier, my biggest fear is that the design-a-exalt nature of Exigents will supercede the &quot;coolness factor&quot; of the other Exted types and players will cease wanting to play the other splats. Much like after Infernals was released, a majority of the fanbase wanted to play Infernals over any other exalt.<br /> <br /> It just feels to me as if the existence of Exigents some how makes Exaltation less special if any tom, dick or harry godling can make an Exalt (and i know this is not literal, but i fear it will feel this way).<br /> <br /> You may not understand that i REALLY liked the old setting and dont reallh want to see much in the way of massive changes to it. The addition of more exalts (exigent, liminal and getimian) feels like a massive change. I for certain plan to read the new setting material and incorporate the new stuff that resonates with me, but for the most part i believe that thr setting material for 1st and 2cnd edition was fine and didnt need changing. It is the mechanics that required overhaul, not thr fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:52:40-08:00","id":416388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents aren't really a collective splat though. Individual Exigents have probably had an impact on parts of the setting. But each one is a solitary hero.* It's not like Exigents will necessarily be working together in any sort of collective like the Silver Pact or the Realm or the Sidereal Exalted. So it's only natural that they would have had less impact on the setting, as they're not working in concert the way that other Exalted do.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to work collectively - its the projection of their individual power (and the power of whatever dragon-blooded, god-blooded, spirit, and mortal allies they acquire) that matters.<br /> <br /> Here, maybe it works better if I model the high exigent scenario.<br /> <br /> Let's say that the Unconquered Sun allocates enough divine fire for 1,000 exigents (nice round number to work with). They start appearing shortly after the Shogunate begins and, gods being the ambitious scum that they are, reach saturation in a century or so.<br /> <br /> Many die, whether in violent acts or due to a short lifespan. Let's say turnover accounts for about half, so that at any given time 500 exigents are at roughly the modest dragon-blooded power level. These aren't a big deal.<br /> <br /> Many are relatively unambitious and settle into long term operations never hitting above essence 4, making them roughly equivalent to the second highest tier of dragon-blooded, let's say 400 more do this.<br /> <br /> That leaves 100 who fully develop their power and live long lives. 100 brand new, each completely unique, elder exalts. And at a stroke I have just doubled the number of non-dragon-blooded elders in Creation. yes some get killed or wander off into the Wyld and stop having influence, but they get replaced by new ones. Each of these exalts is powerful enough, to shape a small society <i>completely on their own</i>. They are probably concentrated in the Threshold in the nominally independent territories between Lunar influence and Realm influence. Anything I put into those regions has to contend with exigent influence of considerable potency. There are now dozens of societies in Creation that have been heavily shaped by exigents for centuries, each one is skewed towards a unique goal.<br /> <br /> Additionally, all the non-elder exigents still count. Every major city that doesn't have powers present to throw them out has at least one in residence, maybe two. There are probably a whole bunch of other effects I'm not even thinking of right now that'll hit me soon enough.<br /> <br /> Could this be cool? Sure, it absolutely could be. does it fundamentally change Creation at every operational scale above the village level - yes, it pretty much does. Is that the goal of 3e? I don't think so, and frankly I hope not. It's a very unstable world, enough so that it vastly devalues the return of the Solars as an event, since with exigents all over the place the usurpation didn't really stabilize anything.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:57:57-08:00","id":416393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not understand that I really liked the old setting and don't really want to see much in the way of massive changes to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your personal preference, and I won't tell you you're wrong for it. However, I absolutely would tell the devs they're wrong if they tried to create a setting that wasn't massively changed, because if they did that, then they would be selling me the same fucking game I've already bought twice, thus pissing me off even more than I already am about the waste of time, money, and innocence I've invested in the line over the last fifteen-twenty years. Fortunately, I think we can both be happy here, since the new material they're including is stuff you can easily exclude at your table.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I apologize if my word choice sounds sarcastic or passive-aggressive. I genuinely will not tell you your preference is wrong, because doing so is ridiculous and insupportable; I also genuinely do think we can both be happy with what comes out, since you're not required to use material you don't want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 02-23-2015, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:34:34-08:00","id":416411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416393#post416393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's your personal preference, and I won't tell you you're wrong for it. However, I absolutely would tell the devs they're wrong if they tried to create a setting that wasn't massively changed, because if they did that, then they would be selling me the same fucking game I've already bought twice, thus pissing me off even more than I already am about the waste of time, money, and innocence I've invested in the line over the last fifteen-twenty years. Fortunately, I think we can both be happy here, since the new material they're including is stuff you can easily exclude at your table.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I apologize if my word choice sounds sarcastic or passive-aggressive. I genuinely will not tell you your preference is wrong, because doing so is ridiculous and insupportable; I also genuinely do think we can both be happy with what comes out, since you're not required to use material you don't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>the mechanics changing so drastically is enough to bring me to the new edition. i consider system and setting to be seperate entities. You dont have to change one to change the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:41:45-08:00","id":416415,"title":"","content":"That's fine. I just dislike buying the same movie on VHS, DVD, and Blu-ray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T06:22:20-08:00","id":416438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416415#post416415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine. I just dislike buying the same movie on VHS, DVD, and Blu-ray.</div> </div> </div> </div>And pay to watch it on YouTube! Additionally, when the technology to beam a movie directly into your brain crops up in eight years or so, they'll charge you for <i>Ghostbusters 2</i><b> again</b>. First you pay to download the movie into your gray matter, then they charge you a monthly subscription fee so they don't delete it (and all your <i>Ghostbusters</i>-related memories). Subtitles, commentary, and other &quot;special features&quot; are handled through microtransactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-23-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:28:40-08:00","id":416481,"title":"","content":"TBH it's just some of the 2nd Ed asshattery that has to be turned back, and maybe the Lunars getting a bump up from their apparent-in-1st-Ed &quot;Lunar Smash!&quot;-oversimplified presentation...<br /> But since 2E actually happened I do agree with the devs that the setting has to be changed, if you go from 2E as the status quo. Move back towards 1E in many aspects, and smooth some edges. I understand that is what is being done. <br /> Creation is huge, a few dozen (or even hundred) more Exigents in the setting aren't gonna rustle my jammies, especially not since there were always uncounted high-power players like spirits, for example. <br /> So I don't really get what meaningful departure from the old setting presentation surfaces when &quot;here be powerful elemental dragons&quot; changes to &quot;here also potentially be exigents&quot; - they're not a unified power bloc, they are probably often times closer to terrestrials in their power scale, and personal power is just vastly less interesting compared to infrastructure and resources when you discuss setting impact.<br /> <br /> So even if there were a thousand Exigents, Dragon Blooded would still run shit, because they fucked the Dynasty into existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:32:42-08:00","id":416482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned earlier, my biggest fear is that the design-a-exalt nature of Exigents will supercede the &quot;coolness factor&quot; of the other Exted types and players will cease wanting to play the other splats. Much like after Infernals was released, a majority of the fanbase wanted to play Infernals over any other exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned earlier this is an easily remedied problem at the table level. <br /> <br /> And the reasons people wanted to play Infernals is that Infernals represented the first splat book with good and flavorful mechanics since the 2e core. Lunars were bland silver Solars; Sid and DB mechanics didn't work well at all - frankly their mechanics were total shit; Abyssals were largely Solar copypasta. Is it really a surprise people gravitated towards the splat with a new theme and actual working mechanics?<br /> <br /> I doubt those same considerations will be present in 3e. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just feels to me as if the existence of Exigents some how makes Exaltation less special if any tom, dick or harry godling can make an Exalt (and i know this is not literal, but i fear it will feel this way).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a zero sum game as you seem to think it is. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not understand that i REALLY liked the old setting and dont reallh want to see much in the way of massive changes to it. The addition of more exalts (exigent, liminal and getimian) feels like a massive change. I for certain plan to read the new setting material and incorporate the new stuff that resonates with me, but for the most part i believe that thr setting material for 1st and 2cnd edition was fine and didnt need changing. It is the mechanics that required overhaul, not thr fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey that's great. Leave out what you don't want. Problem solved. <br /> <br /> And yes the setting did need overhaul--serious overhaul, especially with Lunars, power scope and tech level--but I doubt that it will be hard for you to change the narrative back to your preference. <br /> <br /> I agree with others who didn't want to buy the exact same setting a 3rd time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416411#post416411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the mechanics changing so drastically is enough to bring me to the new edition. i consider system and setting to be seperate entities. You dont have to change one to change the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey good for you. You don't speak for everybody though. The setting was due for some new flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-23-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:37:12-08:00","id":416486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned earlier, my biggest fear is that the design-a-exalt nature of Exigents will supercede the &quot;coolness factor&quot; of the other Exted types and players will cease wanting to play the other splats. Much like after Infernals was released, a majority of the fanbase wanted to play Infernals over any other exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416104#post416104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;This idea is too cool for those dumb assholes who play the game, because they'll just fuck it up&quot; is one an RPG designer must never entertain. They have to credit the people who buy their product with being both willing and able to play the game. If you don't trust people that much, then it sounds like a problem specific to (though not necessarily <i>exclusive</i> to) your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf for years refused to make splatbooks for groups like the White Howlers because they thought special snowflakes were badwrongfun and that the game needed to push players away from that and slap their wrists until they played &quot;correctly.&quot; Finally, the current devs have realized this was dumb and that those decisions should be left to the gaming table. Thus we have books like the White Howlers Tribebook now, and it is good.<br /> <br /> The place for making the decision to allow or not allow a splat is at your gaming table. If it leads to your players detracting from the fun, then it makes sense to disallow it. This is only one of many potential problems that can crop up in a RPG group -- I see gathering a good and harmonious group as half of what it takes to have fun. But that isn't a good reason, by itself, to say Exigents shouldn't be written as an option. Just as it was not a valid reason to eliminate Devil-Tigers.<br /> <br /> I do feel some concern about the possibility that there are 1000 Exigences and they're having a drastic impact on the setting. Liminals aren't likely to make huge changes to history but Getimians and Exigents could, and Lunars and god-bloods really <b><i>should</i></b>, so the setting is going to be significantly different. Whether it's better-written or worse, we'll have to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-23-2015, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:17:55-08:00","id":416502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416486#post416486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf for years refused to make splatbooks for groups like the White Howlers because they thought special snowflakes were badwrongfun and that the game needed to push players away from that and slap their wrists until they played &quot;correctly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and that's not the first or last time White Wolf sneered at its customers. We all remember that jibe in second edition Dragon-Blooded about power players. I think it's been long enough since the last incident that I'd feel bad about continuing to hold it against them, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:40:47-08:00","id":416563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416486#post416486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf for years refused to make splatbooks for groups like the White Howlers because they thought special snowflakes were badwrongfun and that the game needed to push players away from that and slap their wrists until they played &quot;correctly.&quot; Finally, the current devs have realized this was dumb and that those decisions should be left to the gaming table. Thus we have books like the White Howlers Tribebook now, and it is good.<br /> <br /> The place for making the decision to allow or not allow a splat is at your gaming table. If it leads to your players detracting from the fun, then it makes sense to disallow it. This is only one of many potential problems that can crop up in a RPG group -- I see gathering a good and harmonious group as half of what it takes to have fun. But that isn't a good reason, by itself, to say Exigents shouldn't be written as an option. Just as it was not a valid reason to eliminate Devil-Tigers.<br /> <br /> I do feel some concern about the possibility that there are 1000 Exigences and they're having a drastic impact on the setting. Liminals aren't likely to make huge changes to history but Getimians and Exigents could, and Lunars and god-bloods really <b><i>should</i></b>, so the setting is going to be significantly different. Whether it's better-written or worse, we'll have to wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was lucky to play a small part in the decision to push forward a White Howler tribebook, because the origin I wrote for White Howlers was so well-liked by the developer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:41:16-08:00","id":416564,"title":"","content":"Since chatter about &quot;a thousand Exigents&quot; keeps coming up, this reminder seems worthwhile:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke, from the RPG.Net thread[/quote</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">100 Sids and 300 Solars, and around 400 Lunars. Exigents have similarly low numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And eh, why not another on the nature of timing:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, Exigents were well established by [the Niobraran War], and have their origins in the divine revolution against the enemies of the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a couple of other miscellaneous reminders:<br /> 1) Some Exigents have a mode of &quot;transference&quot;/continuation beyond the original. Some are simply of the one-and-done variety.<br /> 2) The Divine Exigence has some sort of connection to the Solar Exalted; &quot;even the fires of the Exigence guttered&quot; in their absence. The implication is that there have been few or none created (or perhaps that those created weren't of the same grandeur as before) while the Solars were out of commission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:44:37-08:00","id":416569,"title":"","content":"Ah, missed that numbers comment. <br /> <br /> Though, eh, I dunno what to make of the &quot;fires of Exigence guttered&quot; comment, their unavailability during the Shogunate wouldn't be my personal interpretative preference. Maybe fewer though as it is such a big investment. I wouldn't be surprised if a lot of gods tried during the Contagion and both they and their Exigents didn't survive that and the Crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 02-23-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:46:18-08:00","id":416570,"title":"","content":"There were low numbers of Exigents in the early and middle of the First Age. By the end they had dropped off drastically, as no new ones were being made. There are likely less than 100 Exigents around when the Empress vanishes, maybe even significantly fewer than 50 across all of Creation. The number is expected to rise with the return of the Solars, but not drastically. Gods who are corrupt, indolent, and wicked are going to need to fish Exigency off the &quot;black market.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:49:59-08:00","id":416574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416570#post416570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were low numbers of Exigents in the early and middle of the First Age. By the end they had dropped off drastically, as no new ones were being made. There are likely less than 100 Exigents around when the Empress vanishes, maybe even significantly fewer than 50 across all of Creation. The number is expected to rise with the return of the Solars, but not drastically. Gods who are corrupt, indolent, and wicked are going to need to fish Exigency off the &amp;quot;black market.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hoping that some notion of how Exaltation can hit the black market will be explained, if only allegorically or in a piece of fiction. Right now it sounds a bit like &quot;exchange this voucher for 1 goblet of Exigence&quot; that gets stolen or sold and passed around, which I'm not sure is the ultimate intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:57:36-08:00","id":416580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416393#post416393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, I think we can both be happy here, since the new material they're including is stuff you can easily exclude at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern is how easily I can put back IN stuff that they're (obviously wrong-headedly, since they're going against what *I* prefer) taking out in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:58:36-08:00","id":416582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I havent forgotten about Getimians or Liminals. I include them in the category unecessary filler. I'm not 100% decided if i dont want to use them, and that will greatly depend on their role in the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As mentioned earlier, my biggest fear is that the design-a-exalt nature of Exigents will supercede the &quot;coolness factor&quot; of the other Exted types and players will cease wanting to play the other splats. Much like after Infernals was released, a majority of the fanbase wanted to play Infernals over any other exalt.<br /> <br /> It just feels to me as if the existence of Exigents some how makes Exaltation less special if any tom, dick or harry godling can make an Exalt (and i know this is not literal, but i fear it will feel this way).<br /> <br /> You may not understand that i REALLY liked the old setting and dont reallh want to see much in the way of massive changes to it. The addition of more exalts (exigent, liminal and getimian) feels like a massive change. I for certain plan to read the new setting material and incorporate the new stuff that resonates with me, but for the most part i believe that thr setting material for 1st and 2cnd edition was fine and didnt need changing. It is the mechanics that required overhaul, not thr fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it works. At all. <br /> <br /> So there's this thing called the division of labour. The basic idea is that more advanced societies develop more specialized knowledge, so a greater number of people work in a narrow field. In less advanced societies, there's less specialized knowledge, so people can perform many different jobs. It's easier to learn all the things you need to do in order to run a farm than it is to learn how to perform brain surgery, basically. At the same time, division of labour allows people to develop more unique identities. <br /> <br /> Not only does that apply to tabletop RPGs, it's also one of the fundamental building blocks of good design. <br /> <br /> In a game with few (splats/classes/archetypes/whatever you want to call them), the designer has to fit a large number of narrative options - all of which have to be mechanically represented - in a small number of boxes. The splats need to be designed to include narrative options that are semi-unrelated, which makes it more difficult for the splats to develop unique identities and undermine's the game's coherence. However, if a game has many different splats, the narrative options can be grouped together in specialties. It's easier to represent these specialties mechanically and it's easier to create unique splats that maintain their identity and that support the game's general coherence. <i><b>Having fewer Exalted is what makes the Exalted less special; distinction is what creates uniqueness</b></i>. <br /> <br /> The same thing applies to charms. Having charm branches with different specializations makes it easier to create characters who possess their own unique identity and who are distinct from other characters even when their general concept overlaps. It's also extremely useful in regulating characters' degree of proficiency. What John said way back when about how Essence 1 charms have a lot of utility to people get more bang for their buck if they want to spread out a little, while Essence 2 charms are weaker on their own, but get really powerful when they synergize? That is a stroke of <i>fucking genius</i>. Dabblers get a decent reward that makes their small investment worth it, while specialists get that, plus smaller rewards that add up to a huge benefit once they put the required effort in. This also insures that dabblers can't overcome specialists, since they won't be able to invest as heavily in Essence 2 charms. <br /> <br /> Adding more Exalted also empowers players by giving them more options. The number of Exalted - no matter how many there are - is fundamentally a mechanical constraint placed on the players to limit their options. Giving players more Exalted also gives them more choices about which characters to play and how to play them, which gives them more power over the game as a social experience. Exigents in particular invite players to take an active part in game development instead of telling players what to do. That is absolutely huge. Tabletop RPGs are one of the few entertainment media that are able to give players that kind of power. Video games can only ever manage the illusion of choice. <br /> <br /> Adding more Exalted is <i>also</i> useful because it extends the game's lifespan. It creates more opportunities to sell books, more opportunities for homebrew material, more opportunities for storytellers and players to expand their games and more opportunities for the fans to discuss the setting. It creates more opportunities for people to take an interest in the game and give it a try. That's really important if you want to attract new players. <br /> <br /> Now, I'm going to quote Pierre Bourdieu's <i>The Practice of Reflexive Sociology</i> for this next part, because it is really, really fucking important: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the social sciences, as we well know, epistemological breaks are often social breaks, breaks with the fundamental beliefs of a group and, sometimes, with the core beliefs of the body of professionals, with the body of shared certainties that found the <i>communis doctorum opinio</i>. </div> </div> </div>Most people don't know how to think. Most people can only reproduce what they've been taught. Most people don't think about how things work. Most people just assume that the world should cater to their preconceptions.<br /> <br /> Most people wouldn't be able to fix Exalted Second Edition, simply because they're incapable of reconsidering the fundamental design assumptions that broke Exalted Second Edition in the first place. At best, they realize that certain outcomes aren't conducive to gameplay, but they have absolutely no idea what those outcomes are contingent upon. The best they can ever hope to achieve is to work around the problem... which only breaks the game even more because the &quot;solution&quot; depends entirely on the existence and continuation of the problem. <br /> <br /> Now, learning how to think is hard. I know it's hard because I spent three years trying to figure it out until things finally clicked. In those three years, I've had several theoretical breakthroughs in my thesis and my comprehensive exam because John or Holden happened to make a comment on system designed that was also applicable for my work. <br /> <br /> The reason why I am unconditionally supportive of Exalted Third Edition is because John and Holden have repeatedly demonstrated that they are able to break with the flawed assumptions of Exalted Second Edition and fix the problems. How do you fix animals? Make them unique and challenging! How do you fix the West? Give it rare resources and make it necessary to the rest of Creation despite how fucking far it is in order to emphasize the historical themes of the West of the Age of Exploration! How do you fix Artifacts? Create Evocations! Expand the map! Add more Exalted! Create new content instead of just regurgitating what's already been done! <br /> <br /> What John and Holden did requires a very rare talent for reflexivity, and it is worthy of immense respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:49:09-08:00","id":416648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416564#post416564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The Divine Exigence has some sort of connection to the Solar Exalted; &quot;even the fires of the Exigence guttered&quot; in their absence. The implication is that there have been few or none created (or perhaps that those created weren't of the same grandeur as before) while the Solars were out of commission.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of this is not that they have any direct attachment to the Solars, other than the metaphysical origin they share in the Sun. Rather, my guess is that when Sol Invictus turned his head away from his Chosen in disgust, lost his faith in humanity, and abandoned Creation to go get wasted for the next ~1000 years, he stopped paying much attention to prayers for Exigence. Maybe his own loss of faith directly made the divine fire itself weaker and less useful, in addition. Probably it took a more impressive prayer to rouse him to actually grant Exigence to anyone. Then when the Solar exaltations were released from the Jade Prison, he decided to give them a second chance and started sending them out and Choosing people again. At the same time he became less stingy with the Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:11:46-08:00","id":416692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416648#post416648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation of this is not that they have any direct attachment to the Solars, other than the metaphysical origin they share in the Sun. Rather, my guess is that when Sol Invictus turned his head away from his Chosen in disgust, lost his faith in humanity, and abandoned Creation to go get wasted for the next ~1000 years, he stopped paying much attention to prayers for Exigence. Maybe his own loss of faith directly made the divine fire itself weaker and less useful, in addition. Probably it took a more impressive prayer to rouse him to actually grant Exigence to anyone. Then when the Solar exaltations were released from the Jade Prison, he decided to give them a second chance and started sending them out and Choosing people again. At the same time he became less stingy with the Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I was trying to keep it a bit nebulous, just in case my impressions are mistaken, though I can also see how my phrasing may have implied a more direct relationship. I was going for more of a correlation, intending one of three things:<br /> 1) The vanishing of the Solars directly caused the reduction of the Exigents.<br /> 2) The reduction of the Exigents directly caused the vanishing of the Solars.<br /> 3) The vanishing of the Solars and the reduction of the Exigents were both caused by something else.<br /> <br /> Unless the setting's changing a lot more than we've heard, I think we can cross off #2 out-of-hand. #1 is <i>possible</i>, after a fashion, though &quot;direct&quot; is probably going too far. Were I a betting man, #3 -- where that &quot;something else&quot; is something like &quot;the Sun's attention/worldview/state of mind/what have you&quot; -- is where I'd put my chips. Particularly given a remark of John's implying that the Sun had a hand in the return of the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:20:16-08:00","id":416694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416580#post416580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My concern is how easily I can put back IN stuff that they're (obviously wrong-headedly, since they're going against what *I* prefer) taking out in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of kicking off another argument about magitech, what are you referring to?<br /> <br /> If it is about magitech, then it's fairly easy to put it back in in proportions to 2e which doesn't really change the status quo all that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:43:55-08:00","id":416708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416694#post416694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of kicking off another argument about magitech, what are you referring to?<br /> <br /> If it is about magitech, then it's fairly easy to put it back in in proportions to 2e which doesn't really change the status quo all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by his <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/407785-if-you-can-ask-the-dev-s-one-quesiton?p=416121#post416121\">only other post</a>, he's mostly concerned with 3ed making theFair Folk rules less weird, and the reduced power-level in the end game (more precisely, if &quot;table-flipping the Games of Divinity&quot; is still possible at some point, which is doubtful if the Incarnae are supposed to be distant figures you don't really interact with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:15:21-08:00","id":416740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416326#post416326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents some how makes Exaltation less special if any tom, dick or harry godling can make an Exalt</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree. There aren't any tom dick and harry gods in EX3. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:21:29-08:00","id":416746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416574#post416574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hoping that some notion of how Exaltation can hit the black market will be explained, if only allegorically or in a piece of fiction. Right now it sounds a bit like &quot;exchange this voucher for 1 goblet of Exigence&quot; that gets stolen or sold and passed around, which I'm not sure is the ultimate intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this isn't supposed to be a flip answer, because we share your concern, but, the frame of reference certainly fits the formulation of the gods being part of a celestial bureacracy with seedy underside, wouldn't you say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:21:58-08:00","id":416747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416740#post416740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally agree. There aren't any tom dick and harry gods in EX3.</div> </div> </div> </div>No small number of tome, dice, and hairy gods, though, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:35:31-08:00","id":416761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416747#post416747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No small number of tome, dice, and hairy gods, though, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Dice God would probably be Plentimon, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:39:39-08:00","id":416765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416746#post416746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, this isn't supposed to be a flip answer, because we share your concern, but, the frame of reference certainly fits the formulation of the gods being part of a celestial bureacracy with seedy underside, wouldn't you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh definitely!<br /> <br /> I guess I've stopped thinking of Exaltations in general--and whatever a god receives when his request for the Exigence is granted--as discrete Things. <br /> <br /> But it's hard to not imagine something like Shady God getting like a box full of Exigence that he would drink or something and transmute back out into an Exaltation which he would put into a champion, but instead he takes it (imbued with his power already), puts it back in the box and sells it, and this happens 3 more times before a god actually sticks it into a person. which sorta seems jarring with the notion that Exaltations aren't really little &quot;physical&quot; things anymore. <br /> <br /> And I'm not sure how multiple gods imbuing a &quot;dirty bomb&quot; would work if imbuing your power into it diminishes you or kills you (as a god) unless it's not the imbuing that diminishes you but the actual Choosing of a champion, as when Ten Sheaves chose Janist. Would all the gods who contribute to a dirty bomb be lessened or just the one who finally Chooses a champion?<br /> <br /> Not expecting a full reply now just things I've been thinking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:53:30-08:00","id":416773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416230#post416230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear that their existence will further dilute an increasingly crowded space of Exalted. There are already hundreds of solars, lunars and abyssals. A hundred sidereals and half a hundred infernals. Then there are thousands of terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Then there are thousands of god bloods and likely a few hundred awakened mortals (though probably no longer a thing in 3rd). The field of supernatural mortals is getting crowded Already without the addition of yet more Exalted types added to the mix.<br /> <br /> What i will likely do with the Exigent book is use it to create customized Godbloods.. I havenalways wanted more detail on godbloods and awkened mortals in general, so that is probably what i will do with that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you to an extent. Personally, I'll run that all the original Exalts and the Exigents are part of my games. I'm undecided about Getimians or the un-named exalts. I have no interest what so ever in Liminals. They have generated zero interest in my group, and I've found the snippets released about them to be as evocative as mud. So the simple answer is, don't include them if you have no interest in them. It's your game, so play it however you want to get the most enjoyment out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:58:54-08:00","id":416779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416708#post416708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going by his <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/407785-if-you-can-ask-the-dev-s-one-quesiton?p=416121#post416121\">only other post</a>, he's mostly concerned with 3ed making theFair Folk rules less weird, and the reduced power-level in the end game (more precisely, if &quot;table-flipping the Games of Divinity&quot; is still possible at some point, which is doubtful if the Incarnae are supposed to be distant figures you don't really interact with).</div> </div> </div> </div>I *literally* found out about Exalted 3rd edition last week, having studiously avoided 2nd edition, and bee-lined for the three things I cared most about from 1st edition - Fair Folk, Sidereals, and changing the world for the better.<br /> <br /> Sidereals didn't set off any immediate alarms - I can't imagine there's anything they can do to stop me from my usual Sidereal playstyle of <i>Better Off Ted </i>meets <i>Top Secret!</i> I'm sure that, given time, I can find some obscure corner of the setting and mechanics that I'll champion to the death despite no one else caring about it. Give me time to assimilate - I don't even know what the heck Getimian or Liminal Exalted are! The Fair Folk thing very well might be me championing something no one but me wants - *I* like it complex, mechanically and metaphysically, but maybe there really are crazy people who want their sublime monsters from beyond reality as it can even be conceived to be simple.<br /> <br /> As for the end-game power levels, if the Exalted killed or defeated the Primordials, it seems to me only right to see challenging the Incarnae as a viable and valid end-game scenario, even if only after literally years of play. The Zenith character in question never actually got to come down on the Unconquered Son like an angry dad on his NEET son, but the <i>possibility</i> helped me keep my eyes on the prize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:16:11-08:00","id":416795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416779#post416779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the end-game power levels, if the Exalted killed or defeated the Primordials, it seems to me only right to see challenging the Incarnae as a viable and valid end-game scenario, even if only after literally years of play. The Zenith character in question never actually got to come down on the Unconquered Son like an angry dad on his NEET son, but the <i>possibility</i> helped me keep my eyes on the prize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well keep in mind that there's a pretty big scope difference between &quot;~800 Celestials and tens of thousands of DBs kill several of the world's makers&quot; and &quot;me and my 4 best buds go pay UCS a visit with intent to wreck his shit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T13:39:06-08:00","id":416846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416779#post416779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the end-game power levels, if the Exalted killed or defeated the Primordials, it seems to me only right to see challenging the Incarnae as a viable and valid end-game scenario, even if only after literally years of play. The Zenith character in question never actually got to come down on the Unconquered Son like an angry dad on his NEET son, but the <i>possibility</i> helped me keep my eyes on the prize.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's still gonna be possible, because it's cool, my (probably very subjective) impression from following the dev conversation (slash hype <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is more <br /> <br /> a) that they don't plan to stat the Unconquered Sun and to instead stat other, new mighty supernatural enemies and build them up as amazing foes... so that the Unconquered Sun doesn't become anyone's idea of the ultimate default raid boss you must level up for years to fight, by sole virtue of being Exalted's strongest statted character, which cropped up more often than it should in the 2e forum conversation. Plus not statting him up means that games can decide how possible he should be to fight / whatever in that game (although obviously canon stats on other NPCs will offer some context).<br /> <br /> (ditto for the Primordials)<br /> <br /> b) the design intends to do away with the idea that any character of X tier is unassailable by anyone of X-1 tier (e.g. X is an Essence Y &quot;Solaroid*&quot; so is unassailable by any Essence Y-1 &quot;non-Solaroid&quot;), etc. in favour of it all being about tactics and strategy and fights being more up for grabs (and so more interesting) between different character &quot;types&quot; generally<br /> <br /> *2e terminology meaning Solar / Infernal / Abyssal you're probably fortunate to have missed out on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:02:53-08:00","id":416868,"title":"","content":"So far we have identified at least two distinct worries about Extingents.<br /> <br /> One group is concerned that because Godbloods (borne or endowed) already fill the role of divine champions then Extingency adds nothing new to the setting, so the effort was wasted on them that could have been spent on expanding rules for the existing Godbloods in the setting.<br /> <br /> Another group is concerned that since Extingents are so new and different that adding them must <i>drastically</i> change the setting or their presence won't make sense. Drastically!<br /> <br /> ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:39:35-08:00","id":416897,"title":"","content":"Exigence giving us rules to craft our own Exalt means we can toss out any splats we don't like, maybe?<br /> <br /> Like, say Lunars don't come out like you want them because after all the back and forth about what we wanted out of the fiddly silver bastards there is nothing that will satisfy all of us at once? Or you really liked Infernal charms being couched in something more nebulous than Abilities?<br /> <br /> Congrats, you got the Exigence rule book! Feel free to ignore the fluff and build you own version of Lunars and Infernals and watch as no one ever uses them because they either wanna use the canon versions, they got their own version they like better or they just don't wanna learn a whole new version because the Devs kept kicking over your headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:37:20-08:00","id":416930,"title":"","content":"Folks seem to be falling a bit into a weird thing where lots of numbers are closer than they actually are.<br /> <br /> From things we know, based on the use of 1e Exalt numbers there are:<br /> c. 150 Solars<br /> c. 100 Abyssals<br /> c. 50 Infernals<br /> c. 400 Lunars<br /> 100 Sidereals<br /> 10,000 Dragon-Blooded in the Realm, probably twice that worldwide.<br /> <br /> From other dev. coments we have seen implicationst aht there are:<br /> c. 60 Liminals<br /> No more than 1,000 Exigents at any given time in history and currently no more than probably around 100.<br /> <br /> I'm going ot guestimate 60ish Getimians.<br /> <br /> This totals to a total Exalted population of about 22,000 Exalted worldwide. Maybe a few hundred more after others are itnroduced. There's probably a simlar amount of god-blooded around. We've been told there's no such thing as enlightened mortals anymore, so toss that out.<br /> <br /> That's about 35,000 supernatural beings. Which is a big number. It's a lot out there! But then remember that Creation on a lot of estimates of prior editions hasl 500 million people. This means that there are four orders of magnitude more total humans in Creation than there are Chosen. In fact, there are nearly 20,000 more total people than there are Exalted. Even if we're extra generous and say there's enough Terrestrials and god-blooded to make it 50,000 supernatural humans that's still one in 10,000. <br /> <br /> Those are actually generally terrible odds for anything. For a vast majority of Creation, meeting any given Exalt is very unlikely unless they live in major settlements tha tend to draw them. I think the idea that we have worries about most Exalts save Terrestrials being counted in the hundreds or dozens as something overfilling the setting is bizrre to me. Excluding Dragon-Blooded, there are less than a thousand Exalts world-wide currently. That's vanishingly rare. One thousand people out of half a billion. In the modern world you're more likely to be a billionaire than any particular kind of Exalt.<br /> <br /> And this is all with an assumption taht Creation doesn't pick up more people in the new edition due to increased area. And Exalt numbers will remain the same as I Note, meaning they're even more dispersed about.<br /> <br /> Whether this is still to many for some folks is one thing, but I am somewhat surprised at the impressions on numbers given about here.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:14:54-08:00","id":416955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416746#post416746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this isn't supposed to be a flip answer, because we share your concern, but, the frame of reference certainly fits the formulation of the gods being part of a celestial bureacracy with seedy underside, wouldn't you say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think the idea works. I don't think the brief description worked very well because it gave a wrong impression, but the system of the Gods in Creation is corrupt and dodgy, that's totally a thing.<br /> <br /> Personally I am well up for Exigents. They seem great, especially for NPC purposes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:35:18-08:00","id":416965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416930#post416930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From other dev. coments we have seen implicationst aht there are:<br /> c. 60 Liminals</div> </div> </div> </div>Where have you heard this number?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thousand people out of half a billion. In the modern world you're more likely to be a billionaire than any particular kind of Exalt. </div> </div> </div>I feel like the billionaire comparison is particularly apt because of another factor: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_the_number_of_US_dollar_billionaires\" target=\"_blank\">neither group follows anything like a uniform distribution across the world</a>. A majority -- or at minimum a plurality -- of those Exalted are Dragonblooded on the Blessed Isle, which likewise boasts higher rates of Terrestrial Exaltation than anywhere else in Creation. Even presuming away Lost Egg and the other Exalted's Exaltation rates as roughly uniform, it's still unreasonable to assume that those Chosen are going to stay where they are. Some will, but some are certainly going to go elsewhere. There's going to be a tendency for these more mobile Exalts to gravitate toward places that have things to offer them -- which may, funnily enough, include other Exalts with whom to ally.<br /> <br /> Just taking the total number of Chosen and dividing them over the entire area of Creation can give <i>some</i> useful information, but it's really important to remember that it misses a great deal of nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:02:54-08:00","id":416980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416930#post416930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folks seem to be falling a bit into a weird thing where lots of numbers are closer than they actually are.<br /> <br /> From things we know, based on the use of 1e Exalt numbers there are:<br /> c. 150 Solars<br /> c. 100 Abyssals<br /> c. 50 Infernals<br /> c. 400 Lunars<br /> 100 Sidereals<br /> 10,000 Dragon-Blooded in the Realm, probably twice that worldwide.<br /> <br /> From other dev. coments we have seen implicationst aht there are:<br /> c. 60 Liminals<br /> No more than 1,000 Exigents at any given time in history and currently no more than probably around 100.<br /> <br /> I'm going ot guestimate 60ish Getimians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of your numbers might need adjusting. First, one of the Devs (can't remember if it was Holden or Vance) mentioned 300 Solars. It's possible he meant 300 Solaroids total (150 Solars, 100 Abyssals, 50 Infernals). It's also possible he meant there are 300 Solars, 100+ Abyssals, and 50ish Infernals. They never clarified this AFAIK, and the whole &quot;forged in pairs with Lunars&quot; is now out the window (which is kinda sad IMO).<br /> <br /> Also, the Devs have mentioned that the number of Dragonbloods is going up a bit from 2E. Their numbers in 2E seemed to change from book to book, but it was generally between 20,000 and 30,000. I would ballpark the number of Dragonbloods in 3E to be somewhere around 30,000.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I'm curious where you got the numbers for Liminals? I would also increase the number of Getimians to around 200. Mostly because I don't think 60 would pose as much of a threat to the Sidereals as has been mentioned by the Devs (they have an established network in Heaven, have several Elders among them, can use the IO to send Wyld Hunts after them, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:59:27-08:00","id":417108,"title":"","content":"The gist I got with Solars and Abyssals are using their original STC numbers. Infernals the fifty they have had since 1e as well. With Lunars implied at those numbers and such, I kind of assume the other original Exalts are as well.<br /> <br /> And while there are going to be more Terrestrial Exalts, I doubt there will be enough to increase it by any significant factor. They are still in all a small portion of total population of Creation is going to be my bet on that.<br /> <br /> Liminals being numberd about 60 I remmber when they first came up way back with <i>Masters of Jade</i>. So these numbers might be fof, but I also doubt they'll be findable again anymore.<br /> <br /> Getimians as I understand it have never been given a number that I'm aware of though, but I'm sure I could have missed it.<br /> <br /> I still doubt there's more than around a thousand non-Dragon-Blooded combined out there. Which again, in a world of at least 500 million in previous editions, is not a lot.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T20:28:58-08:00","id":417134,"title":"","content":"Also, in terms of Exigents warping the setting, it's not <i>1,000</i> exigents. It's 1,000 (or 100 or whatever) peole who may not even know ech other, have no real thematic tie and are as likely to kill each other as they are work together. <br /> If anything, the Exigents are a way to let the dragon blooded shine, showing that individual power is no match for the unity of the dragon blooded host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T21:48:41-08:00","id":417188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416570#post416570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were low numbers of Exigents in the early and middle of the First Age. By the end they had dropped off drastically, as no new ones were being made. There are likely less than 100 Exigents around when the Empress vanishes, maybe even significantly fewer than 50 across all of Creation. The number is expected to rise with the return of the Solars, but not drastically. Gods who are corrupt, indolent, and wicked are going to need to fish Exigency off the &quot;black market.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>wWhy do we have more after the return of the Solars. Shouldnt they be fixing the things the an Exigente would be created for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T22:40:54-08:00","id":417261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417188#post417188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do we have more after the return of the Solars. Shouldnt they be fixing the things the an Exigente would be created for?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar return and the Extingence resurgence is for the same reason; the Unconquored Sun's interest in Creation has been reignited. Now that he's exalting Solars again, he's also responding to pleas to bestow extingence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:15:24-08:00","id":417278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416868#post416868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far we have identified at least two distinct worries about Extingents.<br /> <br /> One group is concerned that because Godbloods (borne or endowed) already fill the role of divine champions then Extingency adds nothing new to the setting, so the effort was wasted on them that could have been spent on expanding rules for the existing Godbloods in the setting.<br /> <br /> Another group is concerned that since Extingents are so new and different that adding them must <i>drastically</i> change the setting or their presence won't make sense. Drastically!<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Idle observation: we're getting books on both Exigents and God-blooded, suggesting that the devs think the two groups occupy different concept-space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:27:34-08:00","id":417282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417261#post417261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar return and the Extingence resurgence is for the same reason; the Unconquored Sun's interest in Creation has been reignited. Now that he's exalting Solars again, he's also responding to pleas to bestow extingence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds reasonable. The Unconquered Sun turned his face from Creation, and now with the Solar's return he is turning it back. That means more Creation gods are receiving the Exigence than there were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T23:54:17-08:00","id":417296,"title":"","content":"So, conversation kinda finished with the revelation that there aren't many of them anyway, but on the matter of elder exigents. What makes you think that it will be common that an exigent will have their life span extended to a celestial level of millennia instead of a terrestrial level of centuries?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T00:02:56-08:00","id":417304,"title":"","content":"Each Exigent is different. Some probably do have Celestial level immortality, or possibly even actual full on immortality, depending on what spirit they were empowered by. But those should probably be rather rare.<br /> <br /> I tend to imagine that many more Exigents would have lifespans comparable to Terrestrial Exalted or perhaps even lower. Heck, I wouldn't be surprised if we found out that some Exigents just have a normal human lifespan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T01:53:23-08:00","id":417344,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, the divine champion blessed with god blooded status through endowment has always been playing the role of an Exalt especially if that deal included an open charmset and excellencies like it did in 2e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T04:56:08-08:00","id":417436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417188#post417188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do we have more after the return of the Solars? Shouldn't they be fixing the things the an Exigent would be created for?</div> </div> </div> </div>This only makes sense if all Solars agree on what the best thing is and all work for it harmoniously, and if all the gods who wants an Exalt of their own agree with the agenda of the Solars. Instead, you could do well to think of Solars as the Unconquered Sun's nuclear arsenal, and once he gets a few hundred world-ending bombs, those gods who don't agree with him are going to want a nuclear option of their own to defend their interests.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:17:45-08:00","id":417473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417296#post417296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, conversation kinda finished with the revelation that there aren't many of them anyway, but on the matter of elder exigents. What makes you think that it will be common that an exigent will have their life span extended to a celestial level of millennia instead of a terrestrial level of centuries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even a mortal lifetime!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:47:06-08:00","id":417483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417296#post417296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, conversation kinda finished with the revelation that there aren't many of them anyway, but on the matter of elder exigents. What makes you think that it will be common that an exigent will have their life span extended to a celestial level of millennia instead of a terrestrial level of centuries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or something even more esoteric, like dematerializing upon enlightenment/death and becoming a hyper-intelligent shade of blue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T11:47:11-08:00","id":417747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416980#post416980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They never clarified this AFAIK, and the whole &quot;forged in pairs with Lunars&quot; is now out the window (which is kinda sad IMO).</div> </div> </div> </div>They also said that the Solar Bond was still a thing. An <i>optional</i> thing that didn't affect everyone, but still a thing available for those who like it. I am satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:02:05-08:00","id":417753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417747#post417747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also said that the Solar Bond was still a thing. An <i>optional</i> thing that didn't affect everyone, but still a thing available for those who like it. I am satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's now the Lunar Bond and it has been implied that it no longer applies exclusively to Solars. Consider the possibility of Lunar/Sidereal bonds or Lunar/Lunar bonds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:22:17-08:00","id":417772,"title":"","content":"I thought there were only 300 Lunars. Did the devs say there are now 400 instead or was that a typo up there?<br /> <br /> I hope that the numbers aren't changed drastically, and that Solars and Lunars still have the same numbers (originally, before the Jade Prison debacle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:23:49-08:00","id":417774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417344#post417344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, the divine champion blessed with god blooded status through endowment has always been playing the role of an Exalt especially if that deal included an open charmset and excellencies like it did in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since 1e, though, I'd seen it done so often. Characters who stood up to Exalted in my games have been...<br /> <br /> - God-Blooded trained from birth to act as their parent's Presence.<br /> - Endowed mortals given a powerful panoply.<br /> - Mortals with spirits locked inside of them who manage to force power out of contract, like living Yasal crystals.<br /> - Spinters of Mokrelus.<br /> - Ochilik\u00e9 (I doubt even the devs remember what these are; much the pity, they were awesome)<br /> <br /> Exigents will... not make much of a difference at all, except to change the classification and diversify the powers of a few of them.<br /> <br /> My Creation was formed in the fires of things like Creatures of the Wyld, it has always been choke full of weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:32:51-08:00","id":417783,"title":"","content":"I doubt that Exigents will step on the toes of God-Bloods much. God-Blooded are going to have their own sets of not-broken charms, which won't be Exalted or spirit charms. They will be much easier to create or endow than Exigents, but probably remain significantly weaker than Exalted.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, are not the &quot;lesser Exalted&quot; occupying a power level between Dragon-Bloods and mortals. Some can be that, but they can also be scary enough to challenge a Solar circle. They will have at least as much range of &quot;power levels&quot; as existing Exalted types, and I expect that practically speaking, any god who goes to the trouble and risk to Choose one will make darn sure their Exalt more powerful and impressive than a mere God-Blood. Otherwise, what was the point of seeking the Exigence? The only time I'd expect a god to bother creating an Exigent who's no mightier than a mere God-Blood is if they're put into a position like Ten Sheaves was, where they're going to die no matter what, but with so little power than they just can't create a very impressive Exalt. Even then, every Exalt is impressive so I don't expect any to be pushovers.<br /> <br /> Note that in talking about power I mean &quot;overall capacity to influence and change the world,&quot; not just &quot;who would win in a white room fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417774#post417774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Mortals with spirits locked inside of them who manage to force power out of contract, like living Yasal crystals.<br /> - Ochilik\u00e9 (I doubt even the devs remember what these are; much the pity, they were awesome)</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we ever get rules for this? It would be great (and possible inspiration for Coadjutor shenanigans for Infernals). They're three separate ways to be &quot;possessed&quot; but have enough similarities that they could share a basic framework of evocation-like charms, or something. Well, maybe not for Coadjutors since mutation stuff fits the Infernal aesthetic better, but for Olchilike and possessed humans and beastfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-24-2015, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:38:19-08:00","id":417795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417783#post417783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever get rules for this? It would be great (and possible inspiration for Coadjutor shenanigans for Infernals).</div> </div> </div> </div>We got rules for the Ochilik\u00e9, yes, in the 1st ed. Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> And the former, as I said, can just be treated like a Yasal Crystal, except without the 'and then the spirit gets free' clause, substituted by something else decided on the bargain (some time free in the character's body? Something the character will do to advance their goals? Go nuts!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:54:16-08:00","id":417812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417772#post417772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were only 300 Lunars. Did the devs say there are now 400 instead or was that a typo up there?</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be a typo but they did say four hundred Lunars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:57:26-08:00","id":417815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417772#post417772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were only 300 Lunars. Did the devs say there are now 400 instead or was that a typo up there?<br /> <br /> I hope that the numbers aren't changed drastically, and that Solars and Lunars still have the same numbers (originally, before the Jade Prison debacle).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is based upon implications that the original STC numbers are about right. There it descirbed c. 150 Solars, c. 100 Abyssals and c. 400 Lunars. Them having even numbers and equal pairing was not canon until 2e.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:00:12-08:00","id":417821,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun made 300 Solars. Luna made ~400 Lunars. There has never been more than 300 Exigents at once, and the actual number is probably far, far fewer than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:05:00-08:00","id":417828,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Aaaaand this sure does look a bit paltry right after the \u00d8-man's contribution. ^_^o Also, evidently Sidereal'd before him, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417772#post417772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were only 300 Lunars. Did the devs say there are now 400 instead or was that a typo up there?<br /> <br /> I hope that the numbers aren't changed drastically, and that Solars and Lunars still have the same numbers (originally, before the Jade Prison debacle).</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's what they've had to say about numbers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John, from the RPG.Net thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are slightly more Dragon-Blooded. Not a lot. 100 Sids and 300 Solars, and around 400 Lunars. Exigents have similarly low numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've not yet heard an elaboration on whether that's 300 Solars originally or presently. At this point, I wouldn't expect that kind of clarification until at least the corebook. I also wouldn't count on the original number of Solars equaling the &quot;original&quot; number of Lunars.* The sense I get of the Lunar Bond** is not that it's something the Sun and Moon put there, but that many Solar and Lunar Exalted grew very and famously close in the First Age (marriages were common), and that the intensity of these associations is what built in that sort of resonance. At least for my part, I certainly dig the change.<br /> <br /> * Presuming there's not even more changing about Lunars than we know about.<br /> ** Which doesn't seem like the mechanically heavy thing it used to be, this go-round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Sidereal'd. 02-24-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:06:50-08:00","id":417829,"title":"","content":"This may have been answered elsewhere, but do Exigent Exaltations 'recycle' into a new host when the current host dies like the Celestial Exaltations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:08:46-08:00","id":417832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417829#post417829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may have been answered elsewhere, but do Exigent Exaltations 'recycle' into a new host when the current host dies like the Celestial Exaltations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each Exigent works like its own particular type of Exalt. Some are one-and-done, some reincarnate like Celestial Exalted, some can have blood lineages like Terrestrial Exalted, and some can have whatever other strange possibility is desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:12:31-08:00","id":417857,"title":"","content":"Does the math add up in such a way that Sidereals can have a Lunar bond mate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:13:36-08:00","id":417859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417821#post417821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun made 300 Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>assume</i> this means Abyssals and Infernals still get substracted from that number, and that the phrasing isn't just a red herring. Given the absence of clear numbers, I guess we also won't be told an exact number on how they are divided between Solars/Abyssals/Infernals (though I'd guess &quot;roughly half/third/one-sixth is still applicable, just not stated as &quot;definitely this round number&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:20:12-08:00","id":417865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417857#post417857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the math add up in such a way that Sidereals can have a Lunar bond mate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Luna made &quot;roughly 400 Lunars&quot;, and since this usually stands side-by-side with &quot;exact 300 Solars were made&quot;, the absence of a clear number of Lunars is obviously intentional. Solars (and derivates?) and Sids together would be <i>exactly</i> 400. Maybe the similarity in number is intentional, maybe it's just a coincidence, but it's unlikely to be a one-to-one match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:29:38-08:00","id":417889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417857#post417857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the math add up in such a way that Sidereals can have a Lunar bond mate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the notion of &quot;bond mate&quot; as a metaphysical concept (represented by Solar Bond or something like it) is a thing of the past. That's my impression anyway, and good riddance if so.<br /> <br /> That in no way means that a Lunar can't have a Defining Intimacy of romantic love or partnership towards a particular Solar. But that Intimacy would be borne out of lived experiences, not because Solar Exaltation #133 was metaphysically tied to Lunar Exaltation #245 in prehistoric times.<br /> <br /> I mean, Lunars were in relationships with Solars. Lunars were in relationships with Sids. Lunars were in relationships with other Lunars. Probably some with DBs and mortals and Fair Folk and etc etc etc as well. Let's not say that one of these kinds of relationships is inherently Better and Greater than all the others, and let's especially not enforce that idea mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:00:25-08:00","id":417936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417889#post417889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the notion of &quot;bond mate&quot; as a metaphysical concept (represented by Solar Bond or something like it) is a thing of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just spend some time on Nishkriya and the &quot;What we know&quot;-Wiki, looking up bonds. There's definitely still some kind of Bond going on, but the details are vague - but it doesn't affect everyone (apparently, there can be un-bonded Solars, and given their numbers, there can obviously be unbonded Lunars), and it's explicitely <i>not</i> a &quot;Brain Lasso&quot; any more.<br /> <br /> The most detailed description I can find would be <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/4510\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, but I think this can be filed in the same box as &quot;Masters of Interpretive Dance&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:00:59-08:00","id":417937,"title":"","content":"The sun and the moon are a metaphysical &quot;pair&quot; in all kinds of mythologies, including Exalted. Their Exaltations are naturally fundamentally connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:04:37-08:00","id":417943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417936#post417936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just spend some time on Nishkriya and the &quot;What we know&quot;-Wiki, looking up bonds. There's definitely still some kind of Bond going on, but the details are vague - but it doesn't affect everyone (apparently, there can be un-bonded Solars, and given their numbers, there can obviously be unbonded Lunars), and it's explicitely <i>not</i> a &quot;Brain Lasso&quot; any more.<br /> <br /> The most detailed description I can find would be <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Posts/Details/4510\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, but I think this can be filed in the same box as &quot;Masters of Interpretive Dance&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, i think I was misremembering about the existence of the Bond.<br /> <br /> I am realizing I don't have that much of an issue with the notion of a Bond per-se, it's just that the 2e implementation <i>really</i> soured me on the whole concept of it, y'know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:06:34-08:00","id":417946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417937#post417937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sun and the moon are a metaphysical &quot;pair&quot; in all kinds of mythologies, including Exalted. Their Exaltations are naturally fundamentally connected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before the forum wipe, I had a signature saying something along the lines of &quot;Sun-Moon Dualism: Accept no lesser substitutes!&quot;<br /> (My relationship to the Solar/Lunar bond is similar to the relationship between a Lunar fan and Lunars: I hated the implementation, several parts of the description, but I loved the basic concept).<br /> I am now immensely satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T15:09:46-08:00","id":418024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417821#post417821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun made 300 Solars. Luna made ~400 Lunars. There has never been more than 300 Exigents at once, and the actual number is probably far, far fewer than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, thank you for clarifying!<br /> <br /> I've long thought that Abyssal and Solar numbers wouldn't be exactly 100 and 150, or divided evenly into castes. I figured that the Neverborn only managed to steal <i>roughly</i> half of the Solar Exaltations and only a roughly even sample of the castes; that the Yozi demanded exactly 10 Exaltations of each caste, or if that wasn't possible just exactly 50; and that the Abyssals were made from the remainder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-24-2015, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:40:22-08:00","id":418250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417774#post417774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since 1e, though, I'd seen it done so often. Characters who stood up to Exalted in my games have been...<br /> <br /> - God-Blooded trained from birth to act as their parent's Presence.<br /> - Endowed mortals given a powerful panoply.<br /> - Mortals with spirits locked inside of them who manage to force power out of contract, like living Yasal crystals.<br /> - Spinters of Mokrelus.<br /> - Ochilik\u00e9 (I doubt even the devs remember what these are; much the pity, they were awesome)<br /> <br /> Exigents will... not make much of a difference at all, except to change the classification and diversify the powers of a few of them.<br /> <br /> My Creation was formed in the fires of things like Creatures of the Wyld, it has always been choke full of weird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Slight misspelling; they are the olchilik\u00e9. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:43:28-08:00","id":418255,"title":"","content":"What are the olchilik\u00e9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T19:44:47-08:00","id":418258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418255#post418255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the olchilik\u00e9?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Kings and gods sharing a semipermanent bond of might via possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:29:51-08:00","id":418289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418250#post418250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight misspelling; they are the olchilik\u00e9. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected, then; on both counts ^_^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418258#post418258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Kings and gods sharing a semipermanent bond of might via possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name means 'Chosen' in their language, it was basically how they had Exalted before the Exalted were a thing (which fits with them being the pre-human mythos, and having a more crude version of divine communion); it is their ritual, and their culture, but it is not just a thing they can do, all it takes is a God who wishes to go through the ritual and have Ride; after all, a Solar Olchilik\u00e9 is what Filial Wisdom IS. I've had fun seeing both Dragon-Blooded empowered to better play in Celestial games, and Mortals empowered to be flavorful antagonists/allies this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T22:33:59-08:00","id":418428,"title":"","content":"I have always run the &quot;Bond&quot; as between Essences who had close relationships in the past. i have never limited it to Solar/Lunar (though those seem to be the most common) but have represented Solar/Solar, Solar/Sidereal and Lunar/Lunar. I would do that so i could have Solar characters bonded with Abyssal NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T03:18:11-08:00","id":418557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=417774#post417774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since 1e, though, I'd seen it done so often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t get me wrong, the generic nature of spirit charms, the fact that the Player\u2019s Guide never advises against god blooded having charms that their supernatural parent doesn\u2019t even know and the whole execution of Half Caste had a lot to answer for.<br /> <br /> I just think Second Edition made it worse by giving spirits ability based Excellencies and their charms no prerequisites except Essence and that encouraged to build a God Blooded characters by starting with an Excellency for their favoured ability then picking spirit charms that be fluffed as an outgrowth of human superlative skill rather than the tools used to administrate a spirit\u2019s domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-25-2015, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:59:26-08:00","id":418667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e#post415418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar cant just sprout wings like a lunar, but he could craft an artifact to give himself wings of essence, or use his charms to just levitate, or wyld-shape permanent ones. Not exactly what you wanted but mixed things up. Its good to have a sense of, you need to work with what you've got. Solars cant shape-shift, lunars cant alter fate, etc. Thus you need to get creative.<br /> <br /> Exigents defeat this. Why think up clever work arounds when I can just have him be a chosen of a god who embodies exactly what I want. No god like that, fine I homebrew one that is and it completely works within the setting. At that point you might as well be playing a free form RP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually 2e Infernals defeat that premise, because they could grow wings as a mutation and still have a dozen or more other ways through which you could justify them flying (or doing any other thing you wanted). The limitation of &quot;you have to stick to your Yozi&quot; wasn't a real limiter, if you could swap Yozi Charm sets, write your own Charms for Yozis, write Charms to change a Yozi's rules, or write the Charms of unwritten Yozis, and you could do all of those things. That's all in a single kind of Exalt.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Chosen of a volcano god, he's going to have lots of variations on a central theme, but you won't see him flying, ever, and many other things will be out of his reach. So what he becomes is an interesting character who fits into the myth of Exalted without actually screwing up the game by bending the entire focus around himself. Since Exigents do not share Charms, their ability to express the setting's myth by way of Exaltation is both refreshing and completely inoffensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:06:08-08:00","id":418673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=415527#post415527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern is that I'm going to run into some player who won't be interested in any of the default splats and isn't mechanically savvy enough to build their own exigent, thereby forcing me to do all the work of character creation beyond the concept phase.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just tell 'em no, if you're not up to that sort of workload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:09:20-08:00","id":418677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418667#post418667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, the Chosen of a volcano god, he's going to have lots of variations on a central theme, but you won't see him flying, ever, and many other things will be out of his reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I've been trying to get a feel for the limitations of Exigents...<br /> <br /> So you couldn't create a Charm that allows you to waft through the air like a cloud of volcanic ash... I assume though that &quot;super long distance jump&quot; charms would be okay though, as you explode up into the stratosphere like a volcanic boulder or what have you, probably leaving a crater from where you were standing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:12:25-08:00","id":418680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418667#post418667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, the Chosen of a volcano god, he's going to have lots of variations on a central theme, but you won't see him flying</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of being pedantic, it depends on the volcano god, no? Because a god that takes the shape of a human-phoenix that trails volcanic ash in its wake might pull off flight (say, a god of morning rooster-calls that got promoted a few times before asking for Exigence), or maybe being held aloft on rising plumes of ash.<br /> Never say never is what i mean :P<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd by Anubis. The forum is having an odd post lag thing again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:25:16-08:00","id":418696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=416582#post416582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how it works. At all.<br /> <br /> So there's this thing called the division of labour. The basic idea is that more advanced societies develop more specialized knowledge, so a greater number of people work in a narrow field. In less advanced societies, there's less specialized knowledge, so people can perform many different jobs. It's easier to learn all the things you need to do in order to run a farm than it is to learn how to perform brain surgery, basically. At the same time, division of labour allows people to develop more unique identities.<br /> <br /> Not only does that apply to tabletop RPGs, it's also one of the fundamental building blocks of good design.<br /> <br /> In a game with few (splats/classes/archetypes/whatever you want to call them), the designer has to fit a large number of narrative options - all of which have to be mechanically represented - in a small number of boxes. The splats need to be designed to include narrative options that are semi-unrelated, which makes it more difficult for the splats to develop unique identities and undermine's the game's coherence. However, if a game has many different splats, the narrative options can be grouped together in specialties. It's easier to represent these specialties mechanically and it's easier to create unique splats that maintain their identity and that support the game's general coherence. <i><b>Having fewer Exalted is what makes the Exalted less special; distinction is what creates uniqueness</b></i>.<br /> <br /> The same thing applies to charms. Having charm branches with different specializations makes it easier to create characters who possess their own unique identity and who are distinct from other characters even when their general concept overlaps. It's also extremely useful in regulating characters' degree of proficiency. What John said way back when about how Essence 1 charms have a lot of utility to people get more bang for their buck if they want to spread out a little, while Essence 2 charms are weaker on their own, but get really powerful when they synergize? That is a stroke of <i>fucking genius</i>. Dabblers get a decent reward that makes their small investment worth it, while specialists get that, plus smaller rewards that add up to a huge benefit once they put the required effort in. This also insures that dabblers can't overcome specialists, since they won't be able to invest as heavily in Essence 2 charms.<br /> <br /> Adding more Exalted also empowers players by giving them more options. The number of Exalted - no matter how many there are - is fundamentally a mechanical constraint placed on the players to limit their options. Giving players more Exalted also gives them more choices about which characters to play and how to play them, which gives them more power over the game as a social experience. Exigents in particular invite players to take an active part in game development instead of telling players what to do. That is absolutely huge. Tabletop RPGs are one of the few entertainment media that are able to give players that kind of power. Video games can only ever manage the illusion of choice.<br /> <br /> Adding more Exalted is <i>also</i> useful because it extends the game's lifespan. It creates more opportunities to sell books, more opportunities for homebrew material, more opportunities for storytellers and players to expand their games and more opportunities for the fans to discuss the setting. It creates more opportunities for people to take an interest in the game and give it a try. That's really important if you want to attract new players.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm going to quote Pierre Bourdieu's <i>The Practice of Reflexive Sociology</i> for this next part, because it is really, really fucking important:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most people don't know how to think. Most people can only reproduce what they've been taught. Most people don't think about how things work. Most people just assume that the world should cater to their preconceptions.<br /> <br /> Most people wouldn't be able to fix Exalted Second Edition, simply because they're incapable of reconsidering the fundamental design assumptions that broke Exalted Second Edition in the first place. At best, they realize that certain outcomes aren't conducive to gameplay, but they have absolutely no idea what those outcomes are contingent upon. The best they can ever hope to achieve is to work around the problem... which only breaks the game even more because the &quot;solution&quot; depends entirely on the existence and continuation of the problem.<br /> <br /> Now, learning how to think is hard. I know it's hard because I spent three years trying to figure it out until things finally clicked. In those three years, I've had several theoretical breakthroughs in my thesis and my comprehensive exam because John or Holden happened to make a comment on system designed that was also applicable for my work.<br /> <br /> The reason why I am unconditionally supportive of Exalted Third Edition is because John and Holden have repeatedly demonstrated that they are able to break with the flawed assumptions of Exalted Second Edition and fix the problems. How do you fix animals? Make them unique and challenging! How do you fix the West? Give it rare resources and make it necessary to the rest of Creation despite how fucking far it is in order to emphasize the historical themes of the West of the Age of Exploration! How do you fix Artifacts? Create Evocations! Expand the map! Add more Exalted! Create new content instead of just regurgitating what's already been done!<br /> <br /> What John and Holden did requires a very rare talent for reflexivity, and it is worthy of immense respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>What an astoundingly sharp read. Your post has also convinced me to go forward with my plan to pitch a book in the future that will involve players voting for Exigent ideas from a pool of my favorite fan Exigent ideas, to be placed in a book with full Charm support as part of the canon text of Third Edition. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:26:34-08:00","id":418697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418677#post418677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I've been trying to get a feel for the limitations of Exigents...<br /> <br /> So you couldn't create a Charm that allows you to waft through the air like a cloud of volcanic ash... I assume though that &quot;super long distance jump&quot; charms would be okay though, as you explode up into the stratosphere like a volcanic boulder or what have you, probably leaving a crater from where you were standing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, 100%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:29:10-08:00","id":418703,"title":"","content":"This exchange between the devs and anubis/fata-ku is a good illustration of what I think is going to happen at a lot of tables. The ST says no and the players who want it all will try to justify it and try to get the ST to change his mind. ST can still say no though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:30:06-08:00","id":418704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418673#post418673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just tell 'em no, if you're not up to that sort of workload.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably what I would do. I mention it only because the mere presence of a DIY option allows picky or obsessive people to take that option instead of going for something else that might involve compromising a little of what they want, and sometimes it's hard to get a game together that doesn't include any picky or obsessive people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:35:01-08:00","id":418711,"title":"","content":"One thing that this whole discussion brings up for me is this little question and answer asked and given in the 'ask the developers' threadnought over at RPGnet<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Jon Chung</i>:<br /> This is not a trap. I am genuinely interested.<br /> a) Is the game constructed such that the most optimal path or the path of least resistance should produce non-degenerate game states?<br /> b) Is the game constructed such that the probability of random newbies hitting trap landmines and having their games explode is as low as reasonably possible?<br /> c) Is the game constructed such that the system is designed to take as much systemic design pressure as possible off the GM\u2019s (untrained) judgement?<br /> d) Is the game designed around the assumption of GM overhead error-correction compensating for a) or b)?<br /> These are pretty important checkboxes regarding whether or not I wanna buy this.<br /> <br /> <i>John</i>:<br /> Yes to the first three, no to the last. We have not relied on ST intervention in the mechanics at any point in the design. </div> </div> </div>Is this still true, given what has been said in this thread? (This is not an attempt to derail or troll, I'm quite serious..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:39:03-08:00","id":418714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drecain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418703#post418703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This exchange between the devs and anubis/fata-ku is a good illustration of what I think is going to happen at a lot of tables. The ST says no and the players who want it all will try to justify it and try to get the ST to change his mind. ST can still say no though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, it'll definitely happen. It happens in any system where players are given the ability to create their own content. I had it happen back in D&amp;D with a player who wanted to make a new spell. I dealt with it in First Edition Exalted with another player wanted to make their own Charm. <br /> <br /> Hopefully there's a section in the Exigent book that just makes it clear that STs can absolutely say no or veto anything if they don't think it's appropriate. As Exigents are going to be a &quot;Make your own stuff,&quot; some ST's might feel uncomfortable with telling a player no, and some players might be uncomfortable with the ST telling them no, so it might be nice if the book just reminds everyone that, if someone's new Charms or Charmset is going to cause problems (or is discovered to be causing problems after it was okay-ed) there's nothing wrong with the ST saying, &quot;Nope, sorry.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:01:06-08:00","id":418736,"title":"","content":"I'm a little bummed by how low an opinion some people (not trying to call anyone out, just commenting on a general phenomenon) have of the fan base. I'd like to think we can trust at least <i>some</i> fans of Exigents to want to limit their characters' powers to a thematic core instead of being Cartman as the ninja Bullrug, whose power is to have any power he wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:13:37-08:00","id":418744,"title":"","content":"Me too. It reminds me of the criticism of Devil-Tigers as nothing but a power-trip and people who want to play them as munchkins.<br /> <br /> Exigents are a wonderful idea. NOT a &quot;replacement&quot; for Devil-Tigers at all, but a very intuitive and reasonable addition to the setting. I remember somebody writing up what were more-or-less Exigents with a different name back in 1st edition and I wish I knew how to find copies of their write-ups online. They were the &quot;Little Exalts&quot; (yeah, bad name) and I think their patrons were Vanileth, Nara-O, Oliphem (not possible for Exigents), No Key, and Five Days Darkness. They were actually pretty neat even if the explanation for their origin wasn't nearly as good as what we got for Exigents.<br /> <br /> Then again I was way younger then so maybe now if I read them I would be like &quot;Nooo actually these aren't well-made after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which, now I have to wonder how each of those gods would convince Sol Invictus to grant them Exigence, and what they would want it for. Vanileth just saying &quot;my purview is tiny now, I want a bigger share of the pie&quot; is not likely to impress Sol. Five Day Darkness might be metaphysically unable to get his prayer heard by Sol no matter how hard he prays. Oh well, there's always the &quot;black market&quot; I guess.<br /> <br /> Now of course what Ex3 needs is descriptions of tons of all-new little gods, including Forbidden Gods, for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 02-25-2015, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:17:31-08:00","id":418745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418736#post418736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little bummed by how low an opinion some people (not trying to call anyone out, just commenting on a general phenomenon) have of the fan base. I'd like to think we can trust at least <i>some</i> fans of Exigents to want to limit their characters' powers to a thematic core instead of being Cartman as the ninja Bullrug, whose power is to have any power he wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Or any number of anime protagonists whose power it is to bullshit their way around all the supposed limitations in their powerset.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:38:35-08:00","id":418781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418745#post418745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Or any number of anime protagonists whose power it is to bullshit their way around all the supposed limitations in their powerset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, but I'm not a big enough fan of anime to comment on that, and I prefer <b>South Park</b> references where possible.<br /> <br /> Am I missing the point by saying that, though? Was your post an oblique reference to, I don't know, to source material giving the fans the wrong idea, or something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:53:48-08:00","id":418794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418677#post418677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you couldn't create a Charm that allows you to waft through the air like a cloud of volcanic ash...</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda want to see an Exigent of a god of volcanic ash, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:56:26-08:00","id":418797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418781#post418781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, but I'm not a big enough fan of anime to comment on that, and I prefer <b>South Park</b> references where possible.<br /> <br /> Am I missing the point by saying that, though? Was your post an oblique reference to, I don't know, to source material giving the fans the wrong idea, or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>My post is intended as an addendum to your post. It is not meant to contradict your post, or to reference anything in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:23:10-08:00","id":418817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418677#post418677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you couldn't create a Charm that allows you to waft through the air like a cloud of volcanic ash...</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine you could do it if you were working based on a volcano god whose powers were based on volcanic ash, but who had no lava-based powers for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:31:22-08:00","id":418826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418794#post418794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda want to see an Exigent of a god of volcanic ash, now.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about an alien Exalt aspected towards ash from a Heavens Reach game? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:41:02-08:00","id":418832,"title":"","content":"This might be covered in the future Exigents hardback, but, who gets to say (in-setting) what Charms the Exigent gets? Are they derived directly from the god's themes and are somewhat set in stone like a closed charm-set? Is it the Exigent that makes them up as it goes along, constrained only by theme but otherwise free to make up whatever works down to any arbitrary depth?<br /> <br /> As in, is it up to the Exigents to figure out how to apply their power (e.g. volcanoes) to Craft and create appropriate Charms, or is there a point where the Exaltation just shrugs and tells the character &quot;sorry man, I got nothing&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-25-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:42:28-08:00","id":418833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418817#post418817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine you could do it if you were working based on a volcano god whose powers were based on volcanic ash, but who had no lava-based powers for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the God of Vesuvius rather than Kilauea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T10:54:15-08:00","id":418949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418832#post418832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be covered in the future Exigents hardback, but, who gets to say (in-setting) what Charms the Exigent gets? Are they derived directly from the god's themes and are somewhat set in stone like a closed charm-set? Is it the Exigent that makes them up as it goes along, constrained only by theme but otherwise free to make up whatever works down to any arbitrary depth?<br /> <br /> As in, is it up to the Exigents to figure out how to apply their power (e.g. volcanoes) to Craft and create appropriate Charms, or is there a point where the Exaltation just shrugs and tells the character &quot;sorry man, I got nothing&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The dev's have mentioned that charms are now just aspects of a character's experience, will, imagination, etc and not things hard-wired into an exalation. (I don't think it was that way in 2nd either unless you were an infernal.) So the hard wired aspect isn't gong to show up and it will probably be closer to &quot;making it up as you go&quot; for everyone when it comes to charms. As for what exigents are limited to I would say they are limited in to theme of their patron god. Though like other exalts this gets tricky since we've had mention of a hypothetical healing exigent. The example there was that while the exigent would be able to heal injuries and wounds, they would also be able to do stuff like heal relationships. So think of it as sticking to your theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T10:57:29-08:00","id":418950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418680#post418680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of being pedantic, it depends on the volcano god, no? Because a god that takes the shape of a human-phoenix that trails volcanic ash in its wake might pull off flight (say, a god of morning rooster-calls that got promoted a few times before asking for Exigence), or maybe being held aloft on rising plumes of ash.<br /> Never say never is what i mean :P<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd by Anubis. The forum is having an odd post lag thing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I missed this post before. It's a really good one! I don't find this to be pedantic, because in this case you are really digging in and defining a volcano spirit as different from one I am imagining, and yet it is quite easily recognizable as a volcano spirit, and therefore yes, your Exigent of the volcano could have flight. Bravo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T11:08:13-08:00","id":418986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418744#post418744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents are a wonderful idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>=D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418744#post418744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their patrons were Vanileth, Nara-O, Oliphem (not possible for Exigents), No Key, and Five Days Darkness. They were actually pretty neat even if the explanation for their origin wasn't nearly as good as what we got for Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of these characters are highly likely to have an Exigent on the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418744#post418744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, now I have to wonder how each of those gods would convince Sol Invictus to grant them Exigence, and what they would want it for. Vanileth just saying &quot;my purview is tiny now, I want a bigger share of the pie&quot; is not likely to impress Sol. Five Day Darkness might be metaphysically unable to get his prayer heard by Sol no matter how hard he prays. Oh well, there's always the &quot;black market&quot; I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very glad I made the Unconquered Sun's plan fallible, a lot of the most interesting spirits are vile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418744#post418744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now of course what Ex3 needs is descriptions of tons of all-new little gods, including Forbidden Gods, for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Edition will be rehabilitating gods into things worthy of being called god.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spirit&quot; encompasses a much broader affect in Third Edition, where any spirit outside the Bureau of Heaven can never be called a god. There are things wandering the tracts of Creation that have never been recognized by Heaven, save to declare them Abomination. Wait til you see some of the enemies of the enemies of the gods. If these are the things which the Yozis fought with and banished, then the gods must truly be mighty to have stood against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T11:11:57-08:00","id":418989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418832#post418832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be covered in the future Exigents hardback, but, who gets to say (in-setting) what Charms the Exigent gets? Are they derived directly from the god's themes and are somewhat set in stone like a closed charm-set? Is it the Exigent that makes them up as it goes along, constrained only by theme but otherwise free to make up whatever works down to any arbitrary depth?<br /> <br /> As in, is it up to the Exigents to figure out how to apply their power (e.g. volcanoes) to Craft and create appropriate Charms, or is there a point where the Exaltation just shrugs and tells the character &quot;sorry man, I got nothing&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exaltation is not an actor unless, in some strange case, it makes sense for it to be one. What's printed on the Exaltation is there in the god's Essence. What comes out is a matter of instinct with most gods, like an oyster making a pearl. Very powerful and meticulous gods known for extreme control and delicate craftsmanship might be able to design Charms. The answer is basically, it takes the shape of whatever makes sense, just like how they are chosen or how the Exaltation passes on (or whether it passes on at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T11:13:26-08:00","id":418990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418794#post418794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda want to see an Exigent of a god of volcanic ash, now.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be an incredibly minor spirit, way below Ten Sheaves, and likely a poor candidate for the creation of an Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T11:30:59-08:00","id":419016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418990#post418990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would be an incredibly minor spirit, way below Ten Sheaves, and likely a poor candidate for the creation of an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect he might be a suitable &quot;donor&quot; for one of those Dirty Bomb exigents, particularly if the architects of said exalt's creation were planning something destructive.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong in expecting this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:06:37-08:00","id":419094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419016#post419016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expect he might be a suitable &quot;donor&quot; for one of those Dirty Bomb exigents, particularly if the architects of said exalt's creation were planning something destructive.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong in expecting this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I'm unclear on the whole dirty-bomb thing. When gods contribute, are they also lessened, or is only the god that activates it lessened? Does it make a ...huh*... does it make a difference power-level-wise? If it costs nothing to &quot;boost&quot;/&quot;alter&quot; the exigency then... how possible is it for a god to sabotage another god's Exigence while they're not looking?<br /> <br /> Like, a Corinth-Peacock-God of an eastern forest, patron to tree-folk, asks for Exigence (heh, &quot;demands a Demand&quot;), can a rival forest-fire god metaphorically spit in it while the forest-god's head is turned to spike the future Exigent's Charms with unforeseen, difficult-to-control and inextinguishable Fire-whirls and Spark-crackers, in the hopes that they take the entire forest with them? Would the forest-fire god be lessened in any way for &quot;contributing&quot; her power?<br /> <br /> * you know when you get an idea in the middle of a sentence, and it interrupts everything you're doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-25-2015, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:09:26-08:00","id":419114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418797#post418797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My post is intended as an addendum to your post. It is not meant to contradict your post, or to reference anything in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, just checking. I wasn't sure how much significance to assign that ellipsis. Thanks for clarifying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:31:13-08:00","id":419147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418990#post418990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be an incredibly minor spirit, way below Ten Sheaves, and likely a poor candidate for the creation of an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it okay to come up with a reason why one god, that might normally be fairly unimportant, could temporarily be strong enough to create an Exigent? For example, maybe there was a Krakatoa-type supervolcano that erupted, and it created such a massive cloud of ash that an entire direction was blanketed for a month. During that time, the god of the ash cloud was powerful enough that it managed to create an Exigent before it found its domain vanishing.<br /> <br /> Would that be reasonable, or would that be getting into &quot;shennanigans&quot; territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:09:00-08:00","id":419237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418986#post418986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Spirit&quot; encompasses a much broader affect in Third Edition, where any spirit outside the<b> Bureau of Heaven</b> can never be called a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Did you perhaps meant to say &quot;Heaven&quot; or &quot;Celestial Hierarchy&quot; or &quot;Celestial Bureaucracy&quot; or something like that instead of Bureau of Heaven? Because if you said what you meant to say, I have to ask why the spirits in the Bureaus of Nature, Destiny, and so on, would be unworthy of being called gods?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:14:30-08:00","id":419249,"title":"","content":"Hey, John? Thanks for coming in and addressing the concerns being put out there. I'm sure you're busy, so I appreciate the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:15:48-08:00","id":419308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418557#post418557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t get me wrong, the generic nature of spirit charms, the fact that the Player\u2019s Guide never advises against god blooded having charms that their supernatural parent doesn\u2019t even know and the whole execution of Half Caste had a lot to answer for.<br /> <br /> I just think Second Edition made it worse by giving spirits ability based Excellencies and their charms no prerequisites except Essence and that encouraged to build a God Blooded characters by starting with an Excellency for their favoured ability then picking spirit charms that be fluffed as an outgrowth of human superlative skill rather than the tools used to administrate a spirit\u2019s domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. That is totally a problem &gt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> Hopefully with 3e's unique God-Charms and Spirit-specific merits, what a God-Blood will have access to will be more connected to their actual progenitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:19:52-08:00","id":419312,"title":"","content":"I never had a problem with Godbloded having Excellencies and leaving it at that.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can do normal stuff but better,&quot; Sounds like exactly what they should be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:26:56-08:00","id":419319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419094#post419094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I'm unclear on the whole dirty-bomb thing. When gods contribute, are they also lessened, or is only the god that activates it lessened? Does it make a ...huh*... does it make a difference power-level-wise? If it costs nothing to &quot;boost&quot;/&quot;alter&quot; the exigency then... how possible is it for a god to sabotage another god's Exigence while they're not looking?<br /> <br /> Like, a Corinth-Peacock-God of an eastern forest, patron to tree-folk, asks for Exigence (heh, &quot;demands a Demand&quot;), can a rival forest-fire god metaphorically spit in it while the forest-god's head is turned to spike the future Exigent's Charms with unforeseen, difficult-to-control and inextinguishable Fire-whirls and Spark-crackers, in the hopes that they take the entire forest with them? Would the forest-fire god be lessened in any way for &quot;contributing&quot; her power?<br /> <br /> * you know when you get an idea in the middle of a sentence, and it interrupts everything you're doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we understand of them a dirty bomb exigence is when multiple gods contribute to the imprinting of an exigence. To use the metaphor John came up with earlier think it would be like if you let someone else take over writing your story/paper/letter/etc. The gods contributing to a dirty bomb would be lessened still, but not as much as if they were the sole contributor. I don't think exigence would be easy for a god to &quot;spit in&quot; to contribute power partially since unless you plan to spit your lung into the exigence I think it would be too minor to have an impact. Second as far as we know gods aren't really blessed when creating an exigent. Basically a god is -supposed - to be given an exigence for whatever purpose and then if it becomes necessary they carve off massive chunks of their power ,possibly fatal amounts, to feed the fires of the exigence and empower a mortal. So no blessings for your hypothetical forest fire god. As for the rest of the difficulty well we don't know enough about exigents yet to know the other details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:20:02-08:00","id":419403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419319#post419319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So no blessings for your hypothetical forest fire god.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said the fire god would get blessings, I asked if he'd be lessened :P<br /> <br /> Edit: Although, if his plan works, the forest fires started by the Exigent might contribute to the fire-god's power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:23:30-08:00","id":419408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418745#post418745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> bullshit their way around all the supposed limitations in their powerset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just Stunting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:29:50-08:00","id":419439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419147#post419147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it okay to come up with a reason why one god, that might normally be fairly unimportant, could temporarily be strong enough to create an Exigent? For example, maybe there was a Krakatoa-type supervolcano that erupted, and it created such a massive cloud of ash that an entire direction was blanketed for a month. During that time, the god of the ash cloud was powerful enough that it managed to create an Exigent before it found its domain vanishing.<br /> <br /> Would that be reasonable, or would that be getting into &quot;shennanigans&quot; territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't spoil future events, so some things I just can't talk about. But it sounds OK to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:31:06-08:00","id":419444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419094#post419094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, a Corinth-Peacock-God of an eastern forest, patron to tree-folk, asks for Exigence (heh, &quot;demands a Demand&quot;), can a rival forest-fire god metaphorically spit in it while the forest-god's head is turned to spike the future Exigent's Charms with unforeseen, difficult-to-control and inextinguishable Fire-whirls and Spark-crackers, in the hopes that they take the entire forest with them? Would the forest-fire god be lessened in any way for &quot;contributing&quot; her power?<br /> <br /> * you know when you get an idea in the middle of a sentence, and it interrupts everything you're doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're going to be a natural at making Exigents, friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:32:04-08:00","id":419446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419439#post419439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I can't spoil future events, so some things I just can't talk about. But it sounds OK to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ha! You guys are finally going to make the destruction of Gem in everybody's campaign canon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:51:39-08:00","id":419470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419403#post419403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said the fire god would get blessings, I asked if he'd be lessened :P<br /> <br /> Edit: Although, if his plan works, the forest fires started by the Exigent might contribute to the fire-god's power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm vision must have been blurred when I read that I somehow read &quot;be lessened.&quot; Honestly I thought it seemed like a weird thing to ask; I just figured you were going with that idea of an exigent being created with the hope that it would eventually cause things to happen that would strengthen the god beyond the weakening they got when they empowered the exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:53:58-08:00","id":419475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419094#post419094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'm unclear on the whole dirty-bomb thing. When gods contribute, are they also lessened, or is only the god that activates it lessened? Does it make a ...huh*... does it make a difference power-level-wise? If it costs nothing to &quot;boost&quot;/&quot;alter&quot; the exigency then... how possible is it for a god to sabotage another god's Exigence while they're not looking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked, didn't get a reply on it. Looks like we have to wait to see!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419408#post419408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that just Stunting?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:58:31-08:00","id":419483,"title":"","content":"Can you explain where you see the difference, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:04:37-08:00","id":419493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419483#post419483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain where you see the difference, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's simply not what stunting does. Stunting doesn't bypass the inherent thematic limitations of a given Charmset. It's &quot;merely&quot; (and I use that word regretfully) a really cool description of an action that, by virtue of its coolness, affords the acting character with a boost to their dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:06:44-08:00","id":419497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419439#post419439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I can't spoil future events, so some things I just can't talk about. But it sounds OK to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps Hamoji's diminishment to stoke the fire of Exigence consumes him utterly, sending his volcano spiraling out of control, such that even the sacrifice of the Feathered One does not quench its fury, leading to a volcanic eruption of a magnitude not seen in two Ages? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Even if this won't be canon, I now have a future plot line for my seafaring game!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:28:09-08:00","id":419520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419444#post419444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're going to be a natural at making Exigents</div> </div> </div> </div>=D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419444#post419444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">friend.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://37.media.tumblr.com/2343e47f063f8801e05281d651ef1382/tumblr_n5lp7bU24e1qe77h4o2_400.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:15:41-08:00","id":419586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cappadocius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419446#post419446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, ha! You guys are finally going to make the destruction of Gem in everybody's campaign canon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even a setting reboot can save Gem, it's doom was too strong and bled over into the new reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:21:25-08:00","id":419598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419497#post419497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Hamoji's diminishment to stoke the fire of Exigence consumes him utterly, sending his volcano spiraling out of control, such that even the sacrifice of the Feathered One does not quench its fury, leading to a volcanic eruption of a magnitude not seen in two Ages? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Even if this won't be canon, I now have a future plot line for my seafaring game!)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In his old age, Hamoji lost control over some of his...functions.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:21:32-08:00","id":419599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=418990#post418990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be an incredibly minor spirit, way below Ten Sheaves, and likely a poor candidate for the creation of an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not the god a single tiny ash cloud. My idea was more... a big stretch of volcanoes in one of those mountainous regions in the South has a semi-permanent ash cloud over it that periodically goes down and chokes/fertilizes an inhabited valley. The ash god is considered a flunky by the Court of volcano gods, the thug they send to threaten the people into praying to them, but he's actually more powerful than any one of them except the big boss of the Court, the god of the whole stretch of mountains. Shenanigan shenanigan, ash god gets his hands on a black market Exigence, shenanigan shenanigan. I'm thinking... Something-something, Bearer of the Cinereous Banner. Or Rider of the Cinereous Chariot? Definitely got to put &quot;cinereous&quot; in his title, it's a cool word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419493#post419493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, that's simply not what stunting does. Stunting doesn't bypass the inherent thematic limitations of a given Charmset. It's &quot;merely&quot; (and I use that word regretfully) a really cool description of an action that, by virtue of its coolness, affords the acting character with a boost to their dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't stunts more reality-warping back in 1e? I think that's something I heard somewhere, and cappadocius mentioned he only has 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:36:20-08:00","id":419615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419599#post419599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, not the god a single tiny ash cloud. My idea was more... a big stretch of volcanoes in one of those mountainous regions in the South has a semi-permanent ash cloud over it that periodically goes down and chokes/fertilizes an inhabited valley. The ash god is considered a flunky by the Court of volcano gods, the thug they send to threaten the people into praying to them, but he's actually more powerful than any one of them except the big boss of the Court, the god of the whole stretch of mountains. Shenanigan shenanigan, ash god gets his hands on a black market Exigence, shenanigan shenanigan. I'm thinking... Something-something, Bearer of the Cinereous Banner. Or Rider of the Cinereous Chariot? Definitely got to put &quot;cinereous&quot; in his title, it's a cool word.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hadn't realized how Exigents would inspire people to make up very cool spirits, but here you are, doing so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:40:39-08:00","id":419621,"title":"","content":"Actually, I suspect that this will be one of the biggest 'hidden benefits' of including Exigents- they give people a reason to think about cool gods, a reason to <i>care</i> about cool gods and spirits in and of themselves. <br /> <br /> Certainly, I never really cared about gods that much in 2e, and what I'm seeing about Exigents is making me do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:42:15-08:00","id":419625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419520#post419520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">=D<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://37.media.tumblr.com/2343e47f063f8801e05281d651ef1382/tumblr_n5lp7bU24e1qe77h4o2_400.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel instant friendship for anyone who teaches me something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:44:41-08:00","id":419630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419621#post419621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I suspect that this will be one of the biggest 'hidden benefits' of including Exigents- they give people a reason to think about cool gods, a reason to <i>care</i> about cool gods and spirits in and of themselves.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I never really cared about gods that much in 2e, and what I'm seeing about Exigents is making me do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! We want the world to be full of exciting, powerful and dangerous gods, worthy of the name. Characters that would be fun to fight, or would be awesome sources for Exalted antagonists or rivals or friends (sometimes all three at once). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:53:32-08:00","id":419638,"title":"","content":"Indeed- I <i>love</i> it when I get character ideas off something published, especially when it's not the immediately obvious one you might have intended. The 'what sort of Volcano God would create an Exigent able to fly? Maybe one based off a Garda bird?' thing actually gave me an idea for a concept I already had (a Zenith Caste with a God-Blooded daughter). <br /> <br /> Kinda how Crimson Orphan Abandonment from the Ink Monkey Bones gave me the idea to play a Crimson Orphan who Exalts herself and now has to deal with the fact that everything she knew about herself was based on a lie, and has to consider what that means for her, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:28:46-08:00","id":419668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419630#post419630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! We want the world to be full of exciting, powerful and dangerous gods, worthy of the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree ten hundred percent! <br /> <br /> Still, brings to mind a discussion we were having over on GitP, in which certain folks insisted that because Exalted's gods weren't these super-omnipotent undefeatable \u00fcber-double-spellcasters, that we were using the word &quot;god&quot; incorrectly.<br /> <br /> I was really sorely tempted to just scream back at them, &quot;Maybe <i>you're</i> the ones using it incorrectly!&quot; And maybe ask if they were even <i>familiar</i> with mythology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Characters that would be fun to fight, or would be awesome sources for Exalted antagonists or rivals or friends (sometimes all three at once). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget lovers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-25-2015, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:50:20-08:00","id":419692,"title":"","content":"I liked coming up with gods... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, the God Of Murder, the God Of Nine Powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:58:35-08:00","id":419717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419493#post419493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's simply not what stunting does. Stunting doesn't bypass the inherent thematic limitations of a given Charmset. It's &quot;merely&quot; (and I use that word regretfully) a really cool description of an action that, by virtue of its coolness, affords the acting character with a boost to their dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419599#post419599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't stunts more reality-warping back in 1e? I think that's something I heard somewhere, and cappadocius mentioned he only has 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about 1e, but 2e's stunts could do more than Zelbinnean recalls. While not too much, and certainly less than cappadocius described, I recall them giving some limited narrative license in setting the scene.* I also believe an appropriate stunt with an attack that normally does Bashing damage could bump it up to Lethal, if desired.** It's been ages since I skimmed the Stunt rules, but I get the sense that bending the basic rules to do logical and cool things that one didn't necessarily want endlessly reproducible was supposed to fall under their auspices.<br /> <br /> I could always just be wildly off-base, of course. ^_^o<br /> <br /> * e.g. if it's not illogical for there to be some crates or a chandelier in the area, a character's stunt could treat them as though they were present, and present they would be.<br /> ** I'm not sure I remember seeing this, to be honest. I have seen a few mentions of Charms that let characters treat their unarmed attacks as Lethal instead of Bashing without the use of a stunt. So it's possible that was... not an air-breathing mermaid problem, exactly, but in that vein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:05:29-08:00","id":419723,"title":"","content":"You could also &quot;pull&quot; a blow to do bashing with a stunt, or parry a lethal attack barehanded with a stunt. Plus, since stunning, Knockback, and Knockdown are all up to ST discretion, a good description is more likely to trigger such, if only because the ST thinks, &quot;Let's see if he's floored by this awesome blow.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-25-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:08:42-08:00","id":419725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419717#post419717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about 1e, but 2e's stunts could do more than Zelbinnean recalls. While not too much, and certainly less than cappadocius described, I recall them giving some limited narrative license in setting the scene.* I also believe an appropriate stunt with an attack that normally does Bashing damage could bump it up to Lethal, if desired.** It's been ages since I skimmed the Stunt rules, but I get the sense that bending the basic rules to do logical and cool things that one didn't necessarily want endlessly reproducible was supposed to fall under their auspices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah well, yes, you do get a bit of narrative license, but you don't get to break basic splat themes just with a stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:13:35-08:00","id":419734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419725#post419725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah well, yes, you do get a bit of narrative license, but you don't get to break basic splat themes just with a stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, a stunt won't let a Solar shoot a mouth-tentacle at someone, nor poison everyone in an area by breathing out a cloud of toxic wood-Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:15:21-08:00","id":419736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419725#post419725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah well, yes, you do get a bit of narrative license, but you don't get to break basic splat themes just with a stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, one might be able to pull off an effect that resembled a weak Charm of one's splat with a permissive ST, but there was a definite reason I noted it was less than cappadocius described. Unless it was 1e being described, anyway. In that case, I have no ability to comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:20:06-08:00","id":419740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419736#post419736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, one might be able to pull off an effect that resembled a weak Charm of one's splat with a permissive ST, but there was a definite reason I noted it was less than cappadocius described. Unless it was 1e being described, anyway. In that case, I have no ability to comment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played 1e for a while, but quite some time ago. I don't recall the potential scope of stunts in 1e being greater than they were in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:48:51-08:00","id":419835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419094#post419094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I'm unclear on the whole dirty-bomb thing. When gods contribute, are they also lessened, or is only the god that activates it lessened? Does it make a ...huh*... does it make a difference power-level-wise? If it costs nothing to &amp;quot;boost&amp;quot;/&amp;quot;alter&amp;quot; the exigency then... how possible is it for a god to sabotage another god's Exigence while they're not looking?<br /> <br /> Like, a Corinth-Peacock-God of an eastern forest, patron to tree-folk, asks for Exigence (heh, &amp;quot;demands a Demand&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, can a rival forest-fire god metaphorically spit in it while the forest-god's head is turned to spike the future Exigent's Charms with unforeseen, difficult-to-control and inextinguishable Fire-whirls and Spark-crackers, in the hopes that they take the entire forest with them? Would the forest-fire god be lessened in any way for &amp;quot;contributing&amp;quot; her power?<br /> <br /> * you know when you get an idea in the middle of a sentence, and it interrupts everything you're doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>This got me thinking, would it be possible for two rival gods of an area to pool their power together to make an exigent, if they alone were not powerful enough to do so? Or perhaps not without being consumed by it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T21:58:33-08:00","id":419838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419835#post419835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This got me thinking, would it be possible for two rival gods of an area to pool their power together to make an exigent, if they alone were not powerful enough to do so? Or perhaps not without being consumed by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why they wouldn't be able to if they can stand each-other long enough to make the exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T22:54:45-08:00","id":419863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419497#post419497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Hamoji's diminishment to stoke the fire of Exigence consumes him utterly, sending his volcano spiraling out of control, such that even the sacrifice of the Feathered One does not quench its fury, leading to a volcanic eruption of a magnitude not seen in two Ages? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Even if this won't be canon, I now have a future plot line for my seafaring game!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit someone remembers that exists.<br /> <br /> I, uh. I've got work to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T00:22:52-08:00","id":419901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419863#post419863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit someone remembers that exists.<br /> <br /> I, uh. I've got work to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'll be in my bunk.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T01:53:56-08:00","id":419976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419312#post419312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never had a problem with Godbloded having Excellencies and leaving it at that.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can do normal stuff but better,&quot; Sounds like exactly what they should be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that even in those instances where it's appropriate for the parents divine power to have translated directly into superhuman ability the spirit excellency <b>really</b> lets that down with its pathetic dice cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T02:44:53-08:00","id":419988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419668#post419668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget lovers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Falls in the &quot;all three at once&quot; field. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:18:41-08:00","id":420411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419668#post419668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, brings to mind a discussion we were having over on GitP, in which certain folks insisted that because Exalted's gods weren't these super-omnipotent undefeatable \u00fcber-double-spellcasters, that we were using the word &quot;god&quot; incorrectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would reply to this point, but Thor has been disrespecting me in my 1e AD&amp;D game and I need to go punk his ass out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:13:13-08:00","id":420527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419734#post419734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, a stunt won't let a Solar shoot a mouth-tentacle at someone, nor poison everyone in an area by breathing out a cloud of toxic wood-Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless said Solar had, last round, chewed up and swallowed a Hemlock Spirit with Ghost-Eating Technique. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:14:51-08:00","id":420528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419740#post419740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played 1e for a while, but quite some time ago. I don't recall the potential scope of stunts in 1e being greater than they were in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stunts were less explicitly chopped-off at the knees in 1st edition. They didn't say you COULD do things, but they also never said you COULDN'T. 1st Edition in general was <i>waaaaaaaay</i> more free-wheeling than what I've heard about 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5154-cappadocius","name":"cappadocius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:50:07-08:00","id":420549,"title":"","content":"The &quot;big&quot; innovation of 2e stunts was making it explicit that a 2+ point stunt would let you narrate a curtain into existence so you could swing on it to kick someone in the face, or whatever. It never really struck me as a big deal, largely because that's how my group always treated things in 1e anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:05:13-08:00","id":423347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=420549#post420549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;big&quot; innovation of 2e stunts was making it explicit that a 2+ point stunt would let you narrate a curtain into existence so you could swing on it to kick someone in the face, or whatever. It never really struck me as a big deal, largely because that's how my group always treated things in 1e anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fae's Wyld Stunts were always my favorite because it simply allowed you to do that plus+++. Swing off a curtain that was there... to the balcony, then pull the curtain with all your strength to have the roof crash down on their heads. I love narrative magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:06:24-08:00","id":425654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/415418-exigents-are-my-biggest-concern-for-3e?p=419692#post419692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked coming up with gods... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, the God Of Murder, the God Of Nine Powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You and me both brother.<br /> <br /> I always loved the potential interaction between gods and exalted. I tend to include a lot of spirit interaction in my campaigns when appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}